{"format_version":2,"reviews":[{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-001 confirms durable retained candidate/readback and reopens the same authoritative bytes in fresh sessions.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Session termination and age do not delete current relied-on content; dependency disposition governs retirement.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"IF-002 complete candidate identity/profile/reference checks precede accepted-save status.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Model write exclusion spans final base/profile/authority checks and exact candidate publication; drift rejects or requires renewed checking.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Durable unresolved-write metadata blocks affected coherence across restart; actual effects are inspected without blind retry or assumed rollback.","number":5,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-001\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Retain accepted definitions beyond the authoring session\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Definition storage Module shall retain each accepted supplied definition with its identity, type, and authored content independently of the originating session, and shall report a confirmed save only when the requested retention is established.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A save acknowledgement without retained content would break later-session reliance.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"A later reader can obtain the accepted definition while it remains within retained governed scope.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-001 requires durable current reliance; the content custody boundary must establish what was actually saved.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineering model authors and readers\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-001\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"An explicitly authorized save of a supported definition is requested.\",\n        \"The originating session ends or time passes without an intervening content change.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The IF-001 retain_definition boundary and retained content in the selected governed model.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Check the candidate/profile/identity against the applicable selected state through IF-002 and retain supplied content through IF-001, preserving explicit outcome scope.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Accepted definitions in the selected model; current reliance and retirement remain governed by IR-003. No retention duration, transaction mechanism, or disaster-recovery service is introduced.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"After a confirmed save, end the authoring session and retrieve the same identity, type, and content from another session without the originating private context.\",\n    \"A still-relied-on accepted definition remains available after session termination or elapsed time; removal requires the applicable disposition rather than implicit session cleanup.\",\n    \"A missing or duplicate identity, unsupported profile, or incomplete required candidate check cannot receive an accepted-save result.\",\n    \"If the base or candidate changes between checking and retention, reject or re-evaluate it; an earlier check cannot justify retaining a different candidate.\",\n    \"If retention fails or effects are indeterminate, identify known effects and unresolved scope without reporting confirmed complete retention.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-001\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-001\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-ARCHITECTURE-PILOT\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-001\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-001 for the proposed MOD-001 responsibility and IR-001 scenario walkthrough. Acceptance criteria are intended observations, not executed verification or an approval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:1b06bdee00ba1323e3ef88fcd3bd580f61d1df954e9393fae91f9101677f0861","path":"design/requirements/IR-001-preserve-engineering-knowledge-across-sessions/SR-001-retain-engineering-definitions-across-sessions/AR-001-retain-accepted-definitions-beyond-the-authoring-session.json"},"limitations":["Design only; no implementation, executed verification or satisfaction. Delivery unchanged.","Model-write adapters/filesystem behavior remain unqualified. Control relevant writers or withhold coherence; advisory locks do not control arbitrary editors.","Actor-supplied exact-content/profile rationale is not certification; unsupported/missing association stays a gap. IR-003 owns history, recovery, retirement and action authority."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-001","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 5 canonical AR-001 criteria; single-owner contribution where allocated.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:7ed00afc1e82ff6fe2e273ccdc6c2d239a3d78ca21bd2db5e560960098090437","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-001-engineering-definition-access/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:89dd5bbc3fa01ee2c8b18a90bddcb9ae5f06246adfcf2d911deec9395f45daf7","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-002-engineering-model-interpretation-and-identity-checks/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c0f370b5564e4e3a7fa5dc00a9276755929c35d0d9793e4c56552d785a5eb9e2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:264c5c99e22837edd8f3b4472a691c9a0c9c1fea05aa13adc7f1e0adc7eb8bab","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:f4725d5e0241b4f19d29689d2654ef746035f3d86404e2a7de323303e4b76ff6","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-001-retain-engineering-definition.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; delivery unchanged."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"IF-001 returns identity, type, authored bytes, references, selected state and declared interpretation context.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Storage preserves distinct unsupported, unavailable, incomplete and failed outcomes with their affected scope.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Unknown/unavailable requested state cannot silently select current or another historical state.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Fresh sessions read retained model files and rebuild disposable indexes without originating chat or process memory.","number":4,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-002\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Retrieve definitions with explicit state and completeness\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Definition storage Module shall retrieve retained definition content for the requested subject and selected model state, identifying its profile and scope and distinguishing complete, incomplete, unsupported, unavailable, and failed outcomes.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"An identity without a state or a partial result labeled complete misrepresents retained knowledge.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Consumers can distinguish what was retrieved and interpreted from what remains unavailable.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-001 requires usable later-session retrieval and explicit limits at the content boundary.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineering model authors and readers\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-001\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"An identified definition is requested in a selected retained state.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-001 retrieve_definition with IF-002 interpretation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Acquire raw content and the selected state's declaration; interpret it with the applicable profile and return recorded content and qualified outcomes.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Supported definition content in the requested scope. Other revisions must not be silently substituted.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"A complete result contains the requested identity, type, recorded content, authoritative references, selected state, and profile.\",\n    \"Unsupported interpretation, unavailable content, partial retrieval, and access failure remain distinguishable and identify affected scope.\",\n    \"An unavailable selected state does not result in successful retrieval from another state.\",\n    \"Retrieval in a fresh session requires neither the originating conversation nor authoring-process memory.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-001\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-004\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-ARCHITECTURE-PILOT\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-002\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-001 for the proposed MOD-001 responsibility and IR-001 scenario walkthrough. Acceptance criteria are intended observations, not executed verification or an approval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:ed45e0f248e77c6f6ab103a85517d95306e6279d96863145897cae2076272338","path":"design/requirements/IR-001-preserve-engineering-knowledge-across-sessions/SR-001-retain-engineering-definitions-across-sessions/AR-002-retrieve-definitions-with-explicit-state-and-completeness.json"},"limitations":["Design only; no implementation, executed verification or satisfaction. Delivery unchanged.","Model-write adapters/filesystem behavior remain unqualified. Control relevant writers or withhold coherence; advisory locks do not control arbitrary editors.","Actor-supplied exact-content/profile rationale is not certification; unsupported/missing association stays a gap. IR-003 owns history, recovery, retirement and action authority."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-002","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 4 canonical AR-002 criteria; single-owner contribution where allocated.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:7ed00afc1e82ff6fe2e273ccdc6c2d239a3d78ca21bd2db5e560960098090437","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-001-engineering-definition-access/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:89dd5bbc3fa01ee2c8b18a90bddcb9ae5f06246adfcf2d911deec9395f45daf7","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-002-engineering-model-interpretation-and-identity-checks/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c0f370b5564e4e3a7fa5dc00a9276755929c35d0d9793e4c56552d785a5eb9e2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:264c5c99e22837edd8f3b4472a691c9a0c9c1fea05aa13adc7f1e0adc7eb8bab","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7560d10784271c838deed35d3cd28879bfc4a5789a4d4324c0ea1db3bae8f842","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-004-retrieve-engineering-definition-from-selected-model-state.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; delivery unchanged."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"IF-002 check_candidate_identities rejects absent or blank identities.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Candidate checking compares distinct records across names, types and physical locations.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Equal names remain valid when identities differ; names never substitute for designation.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Missing/uninterpretable required members yield incomplete findings bound to candidate/state, not model-wide uniqueness.","number":4,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-003\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Check candidate identities over an explicit model scope\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Interpretation and validation Module shall report missing identities and identities shared by distinct entities in a supplied candidate model, and shall claim model-wide identity uniqueness only after inspecting the complete required scope.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A partial or name-based check can accept conflicting engineering identities.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Identity findings establish the inspected candidate scope and expose missing or conflicting identities.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-002 assigns uniqueness to entity identities independently of names, types, and locations.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineering model authors and readers\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-003\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A candidate model or definition change requires identity checking.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-002 check_candidate_identities.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Compare explicit identities across the supplied candidate view and return state-bound findings and completeness separately.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Identity presence and uniqueness only; broader conformance, engineering adequacy, and approval are separate conclusions.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"An entity with no nonblank identity is identified as invalid for identity purposes.\",\n    \"Distinct entities with the same identity are reported as a conflict even when their names, types, or locations differ.\",\n    \"Equal names with distinct identities are permitted.\",\n    \"Unavailable portions produce an incomplete result rather than model-wide uniqueness; findings identify the inspected candidate state.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-003\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-002\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-ARCHITECTURE-PILOT\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-003\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-002 for the proposed MOD-003 responsibility and IR-001 scenario walkthrough. Acceptance criteria are intended observations, not executed verification or an approval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:47efc8fa6fe91e2947a1ac3fdd1a5dbb4a8328e4e89ec5dd16589def6703e104","path":"design/requirements/IR-001-preserve-engineering-knowledge-across-sessions/SR-002-unambiguous-entity-identity/AR-003-check-candidate-identities-over-an-explicit-model-scope.json"},"limitations":["Design only; no implementation, executed verification or satisfaction. Delivery unchanged.","Model-write adapters/filesystem behavior remain unqualified. Control relevant writers or withhold coherence; advisory locks do not control arbitrary editors.","Actor-supplied exact-content/profile rationale is not certification; unsupported/missing association stays a gap. IR-003 owns history, recovery, retirement and action authority."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-003","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 4 canonical AR-003 criteria; single-owner contribution where allocated.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:7ed00afc1e82ff6fe2e273ccdc6c2d239a3d78ca21bd2db5e560960098090437","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-001-engineering-definition-access/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:89dd5bbc3fa01ee2c8b18a90bddcb9ae5f06246adfcf2d911deec9395f45daf7","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-002-engineering-model-interpretation-and-identity-checks/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c0f370b5564e4e3a7fa5dc00a9276755929c35d0d9793e4c56552d785a5eb9e2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:3df0b81ddc90cf5abc6d4b8f8239e75a70a11e7ede9bc3de74ec1ce0e966f67f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-003-engineering-model-conformance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:e3fa23aeb0b639459320519bf9a382f1ee11c7696fce1f76c2b420c8cf061d1c","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-002-check-entity-identity-presence-and-uniqueness.json"},{"identity":"sha256:4917081e867bd98336b3da64e9208e06f5ad5c31b78754b209dfb334e5910c61","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-003-engineering-model-conformance/conformance-and-migration.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered; delivery unchanged."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"IF-001 resolves IDs against complete captured membership and returns the unique reference with its state.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Complete zero-match inspection yields absence; multiple matches yield ambiguity without arbitrary selection.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Unparseable or inaccessible required members prevent both complete absence and false unique-match results.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"State-bound identity indexes are rebuilt from authoritative IDs, independently of changed names or paths.","number":4,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-004\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Resolve identities without hiding absence or ambiguity\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Definition storage Module shall resolve a requested identity to a unique entity reference in the selected model state only when the inspected scope establishes uniqueness, and shall distinguish absence, ambiguity, and inability to inspect that scope.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"An arbitrary match or false absence can misdirect every dependent engineering relationship.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"A caller obtains an unambiguous state-scoped designation or an honest unresolved outcome.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-002 requires identity-based designation to distinguish entities regardless of display labels.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineering model authors and readers\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-001\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A caller requests an entity by its stable identity.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-001 resolve_entity.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Resolve interpreted identity-bearing content in the selected state and qualify the result by inspection scope.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"One selected governed model/state at a time; no display-name fallback or cross-state substitution.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"A unique match returns its stable identity reference and selected state.\",\n    \"No match in completely inspected scope returns absence; multiple matching entities return ambiguity without selecting one.\",\n    \"Unavailable, unsupported, partial, or failed inspection does not return a false absence or unique match.\",\n    \"Changing display names or physical locations does not change the identity-based designation of the same entity.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-001\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-003\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-ARCHITECTURE-PILOT\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-004\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-002 for the proposed MOD-001 responsibility and IR-001 scenario walkthrough. Acceptance criteria are intended observations, not executed verification or an approval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:2e698cfd16e79197efd1204c4c5429167345cbf56e2b4a3581350b695be27665","path":"design/requirements/IR-001-preserve-engineering-knowledge-across-sessions/SR-002-unambiguous-entity-identity/AR-004-resolve-identities-without-hiding-absence-or-ambiguity.json"},"limitations":["Design only; no implementation, executed verification or satisfaction. Delivery unchanged.","Model-write adapters/filesystem behavior remain unqualified. Control relevant writers or withhold coherence; advisory locks do not control arbitrary editors.","Actor-supplied exact-content/profile rationale is not certification; unsupported/missing association stays a gap. IR-003 owns history, recovery, retirement and action authority."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-004","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 4 canonical AR-004 criteria; single-owner contribution where allocated.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:7ed00afc1e82ff6fe2e273ccdc6c2d239a3d78ca21bd2db5e560960098090437","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-001-engineering-definition-access/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:89dd5bbc3fa01ee2c8b18a90bddcb9ae5f06246adfcf2d911deec9395f45daf7","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-002-engineering-model-interpretation-and-identity-checks/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c0f370b5564e4e3a7fa5dc00a9276755929c35d0d9793e4c56552d785a5eb9e2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:264c5c99e22837edd8f3b4472a691c9a0c9c1fea05aa13adc7f1e0adc7eb8bab","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:df135bcb902ffda46dbd2f735a38623cceeee5850c9c98857bf8e928c9b93f4d","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-003-resolve-engineering-entity-by-stable-id.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; delivery unchanged."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-002 forms same-ID name, content and same-parent location candidates including moved descendants and reference reconciliation.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Identity replacement, split/merge, collision and semantic reparenting are explicit unsupported/conflict outcomes for this operation.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"MOD-001 rechecks actual base/candidate under exclusion; intervening edits require reconciliation before retaining.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Result preserves known partial effects and unresolved membership; stable ID supplies no renewed approval or evidence applicability.","number":4,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-005\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Preserve identity when applying supported definition revisions\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Definition editing Module shall preserve the resolved entity identity through supported same-entity name, location, and definition revisions, submitting the explicit candidate and base state for checked retention and reporting the actual resulting outcome.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A rename or move can accidentally replace identity or alter semantic containment.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Supported revisions evolve the same entity while existing identity references keep their designation.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-003 separates stable identity from changing labels, locations, and authored content.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineering model authors and readers\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-002\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"An authorized same-entity rename, location change, or definition edit is requested.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The authoring responsibility using IF-001 and IF-002.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Resolve the original subject, form the same-identity candidate, check its identity conditions, and submit it with the expected base to retention.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Same-entity edits within the governed model and preserved containment parentage; splits, merges, identity reuse, and semantic reparenting are outside this operation.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"For supported name, location, and definition changes, the retained result has the original identity and existing identity references designate it.\",\n    \"A proposed identity replacement, conflicting target, unsupported split/merge, or containment-parent change receives an explicit unsupported/conflict outcome rather than a successful same-entity revision.\",\n    \"A changed base state or candidate must be reconciled before using previous findings; do not overwrite an intervening definition using stale selection.\",\n    \"Incomplete or failed retention is reported with known effects; preservation of identity does not renew approval or evidence applicability.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-002\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-005\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-ARCHITECTURE-PILOT\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-005\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-003 for the proposed MOD-002 responsibility and IR-001 scenario walkthrough. Acceptance criteria are intended observations, not executed verification or an approval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:0b6d193cf874537ad68e03df84b6796763572c2a541210f1b75cba2f0631e941","path":"design/requirements/IR-001-preserve-engineering-knowledge-across-sessions/SR-003-preserve-identity-through-entity-evolution/AR-005-preserve-identity-when-applying-supported-definition-revisions.json"},"limitations":["Design only; no implementation, executed verification or satisfaction. Delivery unchanged.","Model-write adapters/filesystem behavior remain unqualified. Control relevant writers or withhold coherence; advisory locks do not control arbitrary editors.","Actor-supplied exact-content/profile rationale is not certification; unsupported/missing association stays a gap. IR-003 owns history, recovery, retirement and action authority."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-005","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 4 canonical AR-005 criteria; single-owner contribution where allocated.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:7ed00afc1e82ff6fe2e273ccdc6c2d239a3d78ca21bd2db5e560960098090437","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-001-engineering-definition-access/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:89dd5bbc3fa01ee2c8b18a90bddcb9ae5f06246adfcf2d911deec9395f45daf7","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-002-engineering-model-interpretation-and-identity-checks/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c0f370b5564e4e3a7fa5dc00a9276755929c35d0d9793e4c56552d785a5eb9e2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:6d1115211378f3b231a2127484f809fb5fa67b16a9986f082275e07d690882df","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-002-engineering-model-authoring/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8660c0b4e3d969b44be6dd640f3a2d9ff4ad81c2d0202ea4ba6c33900ed0dd00","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-005-revise-engineering-entity-while-preserving-identity.json"},{"identity":"sha256:96441c50dce42b25ad8992615c0a75370e6c89072694171a7491fa6caa2867d7","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-002-engineering-model-authoring/README.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered; delivery unchanged."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-001 reads current authored content/references directly without Change history or conversations.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Required unavailable content/reference scope is returned as a limitation without inferred reconstruction.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Optional history is independently reported and cannot hide complete current content.","number":3,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-006\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Expose current authoritative content without history replay\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Definition storage Module shall expose the selected current definition and its recorded authoritative references directly from current engineering content, without requiring reconstruction from historical Changes or private conversations.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A current definition spread only across change deltas cannot be independently understood.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Presentation can access a self-contained current definition and the references it requires.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-004 requires current understanding to start from current authoritative information.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineering model authors and readers\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-001\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A reader requests the current definition after one or more engineering changes.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-001 retrieve_definition and retrieval of its required references in the same selected state.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Return authoritative current content and references with explicit completeness, retaining state consistency across related retrievals.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Required current definition context; optional history is additional explanation rather than a substitute source.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"A definition evolved through several Changes is retrievable with its authoritative references without reading or replaying those Changes.\",\n    \"Missing required current content or references is exposed as a limitation instead of reconstructed as an asserted current fact.\",\n    \"Optional historical material being absent does not itself make an otherwise complete current definition unavailable.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-001\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-004\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-ARCHITECTURE-PILOT\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-006\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-004 for the proposed MOD-001 responsibility and IR-001 scenario walkthrough. Acceptance criteria are intended observations, not executed verification or an approval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:6e2776414fdd6a37236d5a58e2cd72edcc99d87b3fcbb3e1ce3029b2de624b8c","path":"design/requirements/IR-001-preserve-engineering-knowledge-across-sessions/SR-004-understand-current-definitions-without-history-replay/AR-006-expose-current-authoritative-content-without-history-replay.json"},"limitations":["Design only; no implementation, executed verification or satisfaction. Delivery unchanged.","Model-write adapters/filesystem behavior remain unqualified. Control relevant writers or withhold coherence; advisory locks do not control arbitrary editors.","Actor-supplied exact-content/profile rationale is not certification; unsupported/missing association stays a gap. IR-003 owns history, recovery, retirement and action authority."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-006","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 3 canonical AR-006 criteria; single-owner contribution where allocated.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:7ed00afc1e82ff6fe2e273ccdc6c2d239a3d78ca21bd2db5e560960098090437","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-001-engineering-definition-access/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:89dd5bbc3fa01ee2c8b18a90bddcb9ae5f06246adfcf2d911deec9395f45daf7","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-002-engineering-model-interpretation-and-identity-checks/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c0f370b5564e4e3a7fa5dc00a9276755929c35d0d9793e4c56552d785a5eb9e2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:264c5c99e22837edd8f3b4472a691c9a0c9c1fea05aa13adc7f1e0adc7eb8bab","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7560d10784271c838deed35d3cd28879bfc4a5789a4d4324c0ea1db3bae8f842","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-004-retrieve-engineering-definition-from-selected-model-state.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; delivery unchanged."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-004 presents obligations, capabilities, behavior and responsibility with current authoritative references appropriate to entity type.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Available content remains visible while required context gaps prevent complete-context claims.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Optional-history absence is separated from current definition and required context completeness.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Composition uses one captured state/profile; state changes require a new view rather than mixed results.","number":4,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-007\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Present current meaning with explicit context gaps\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Views and traceability Module shall present the selected current definition and its authoritative references in a form that exposes its engineering meaning, while distinguishing missing required context from unavailable optional history.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Correctly retrieved fields can still be presented as a misleading complete or history-dependent account.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"A reader can explain the entity's current meaning and recognize the exact limits of the available account.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-004 requires understandable current information, not merely a successful content fetch.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineering model authors and readers\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-004\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A reader inspects a current engineering definition.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The context presentation responsibility consuming IF-001.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Compose the definition and required referenced content for one selected state; preserve individual retrieval outcomes and explain gaps.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Meaning and current-context completeness for the selected entity; no particular UI or rendering technology is prescribed.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Using the presented content and current authoritative references, a reader can explain the entity's obligation, capability, behavior, or responsibility as appropriate to its type.\",\n    \"Required missing context is identified while available content remains visible; partial context is not labeled complete.\",\n    \"Unavailable optional historical explanation is shown separately and does not prevent understanding a complete current definition.\",\n    \"Results from different selected states are not silently merged into a complete current account.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-004\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-007\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-ARCHITECTURE-PILOT\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-007\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-004 for the proposed MOD-004 responsibility and IR-001 scenario walkthrough. Acceptance criteria are intended observations, not executed verification or an approval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:38f4a6afada36f8ba2852e9efe2a834bdd242a117717024ee65a6c72e0a9f67a","path":"design/requirements/IR-001-preserve-engineering-knowledge-across-sessions/SR-004-understand-current-definitions-without-history-replay/AR-007-present-current-meaning-with-explicit-context-gaps.json"},"limitations":["Design only; this judgment does not assess implementation, executed verification or requirement satisfaction.","Model-write adapters/filesystem behavior remain unqualified. Control relevant writers or withhold coherence; advisory locks do not control arbitrary editors.","Actor-supplied exact-content/profile rationale is not certification; unsupported/missing association stays a gap. IR-003 owns history, recovery, retirement and action authority."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T12:12:35Z","requirement":"AR-007","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"evaluation-implementation-design"},"scope":"All 4 canonical AR-007 criteria; single-owner contribution where allocated.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:7ed00afc1e82ff6fe2e273ccdc6c2d239a3d78ca21bd2db5e560960098090437","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-001-engineering-definition-access/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:89dd5bbc3fa01ee2c8b18a90bddcb9ae5f06246adfcf2d911deec9395f45daf7","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-002-engineering-model-interpretation-and-identity-checks/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c0f370b5564e4e3a7fa5dc00a9276755929c35d0d9793e4c56552d785a5eb9e2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:aa5307eebf251ad71ac5200d76509e3666fad4fccd89384fc189364bd7a12e10","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-004-engineering-context-and-traceability/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:2469f00338b83e9a8a666c90c83cb079a52ea834241f9d0ec01c010066a50951","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-007-present-current-engineering-definition-and-applicable-rationale.json"},{"identity":"sha256:705977004fbc8037699b3af0210641e5ebef9b8404abe990e9e2bc55d2520e5f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-004-engineering-context-and-traceability/README.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered; Implementation and Verification are assessed separately."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"Rationale custody preserves five fields, locator, exact definition/profile association and actor basis across sessions.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Current model references keep relied-on rationale accessible independently of compacted Change explanations.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Missing fields, failed writes and unresolved locators/associations withhold complete accessible-rationale status.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"An association remains attributable to its original content/profile; a changed definition needs explicit new actor disposition.","number":4,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-008\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Retain decision reasoning and its definition association\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Definition storage Module shall retain recorded decision context, chosen outcome, rationale, alternatives, and consequences with their definition association and basis, keeping still-applicable reasoning accessible from current content and exposing missing or unresolved associations.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Reasoning can disappear with a Change record or be incorrectly reused after a definition evolves.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Readers can access the recorded reasoning relied on by the selected definition without invented explanations.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-005 requires durable, accessible, applicable recorded reasoning independently of its originating Change explanation.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineering model authors and readers\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-001\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"Decision reasoning is explicitly supplied for a selected definition.\",\n        \"That reasoning remains relied on after the originating Change explanation leaves current working material.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-001 retain_rationale and retrieve_rationale.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Preserve supplied reasoning and state-scoped associations, and retrieve them through current authoritative references with separate availability and applicability results.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Recorded decision reasoning still relied upon by current definitions; unrelated historical rationale and unrecorded justification cannot fill a gap.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"After retention and a new session, all recorded decision details and their association basis can be retrieved through the selected definition.\",\n    \"Removing the originating Change explanation from current working material does not remove reasoning still relied on by current definitions.\",\n    \"Missing details, failed retention, or unresolved associations remain explicit and do not receive a complete accessible-reasoning result.\",\n    \"A changed definition state does not silently acquire a prior association; the retained association basis and selected state remain distinguishable.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-001\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-006\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-ARCHITECTURE-PILOT\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-008\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-005 for the proposed MOD-001 responsibility and IR-001 scenario walkthrough. Acceptance criteria are intended observations, not executed verification or an approval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:4f3f0e177e943c01dffb6138a7372d2eba28dacf7085253942b4d087d5a8b905","path":"design/requirements/IR-001-preserve-engineering-knowledge-across-sessions/SR-005-retain-applicable-decision-rationale/AR-008-retain-decision-reasoning-and-its-definition-association.json"},"limitations":["Design only; no implementation, executed verification or satisfaction. Delivery unchanged.","Model-write adapters/filesystem behavior remain unqualified. Control relevant writers or withhold coherence; advisory locks do not control arbitrary editors.","Actor-supplied exact-content/profile rationale is not certification; unsupported/missing association stays a gap. IR-003 owns history, recovery, retirement and action authority."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-008","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 4 canonical AR-008 criteria; single-owner contribution where allocated.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:7ed00afc1e82ff6fe2e273ccdc6c2d239a3d78ca21bd2db5e560960098090437","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-001-engineering-definition-access/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:89dd5bbc3fa01ee2c8b18a90bddcb9ae5f06246adfcf2d911deec9395f45daf7","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-002-engineering-model-interpretation-and-identity-checks/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c0f370b5564e4e3a7fa5dc00a9276755929c35d0d9793e4c56552d785a5eb9e2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:264c5c99e22837edd8f3b4472a691c9a0c9c1fea05aa13adc7f1e0adc7eb8bab","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:44ba17cf90ab0805af6fc8fd49d476d5e412fb9f345b8b9ae71f134551067958","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-006-retain-applicable-decision-rationale.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; delivery unchanged."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-004 presents actual recorded fields with exact associated definition/profile and author-supplied applicability scope.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Complete definition content stays visible while unavailable rationale is a separate explanatory-context gap.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Other-state rationale is historical or unresolved unless a recorded applicable association is supplied.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Empty retrieval cannot establish that rationale is unnecessary; missing reasoning is never invented.","number":4,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-009\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Present applicable rationale separately from definition completeness\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Views and traceability Module shall present only recorded reasoning with an applicable association to the selected definition as its current rationale, exposing missing, incomplete, or unresolved reasoning separately from definition completeness.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A complete definition may be confused with a complete explanation, or unrelated reasoning may be displayed as its basis.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"A reader sees the available definition, the actual recorded reasoning, and any association or explanation gap.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-005 requires accessible applicable reasoning and forbids presenting unrecorded or unrelated explanations as the current basis.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineering model authors and readers\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-004\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A reader inspects a definition and its decision context, including after that definition evolves.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"Context presentation consuming IF-001 definition and rationale results.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Use the selected definition's recorded association and basis, preserving state, availability, completeness, and applicability distinctions.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Recorded reasoning for the selected definition; presentation does not certify a decision or establish requirement satisfaction.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Applicable recorded decision details are presented with their association basis.\",\n    \"A complete definition with missing rationale remains visible as a complete definition with a separate reasoning gap.\",\n    \"Reasoning associated with another state is not silently relabeled as current; unresolved applicability is explicit.\",\n    \"No rationale obtained is not presented as proof that no rationale is required, and missing reasoning is never invented.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-004\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-007\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-ARCHITECTURE-PILOT\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-009\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-005 for the proposed MOD-004 responsibility and IR-001 scenario walkthrough. Acceptance criteria are intended observations, not executed verification or an approval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:87e292d1ec9678d8e04a417bfb82a198048a25c95e7cdfe48f0e7aebd62e501d","path":"design/requirements/IR-001-preserve-engineering-knowledge-across-sessions/SR-005-retain-applicable-decision-rationale/AR-009-present-applicable-rationale-separately-from-definition-completeness.json"},"limitations":["Design only; this judgment does not assess implementation, executed verification or requirement satisfaction.","Model-write adapters/filesystem behavior remain unqualified. Control relevant writers or withhold coherence; advisory locks do not control arbitrary editors.","Actor-supplied exact-content/profile rationale is not certification; unsupported/missing association stays a gap. IR-003 owns history, recovery, retirement and action authority."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T12:12:35Z","requirement":"AR-009","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"evaluation-implementation-design"},"scope":"All 4 canonical AR-009 criteria; single-owner contribution where allocated.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:7ed00afc1e82ff6fe2e273ccdc6c2d239a3d78ca21bd2db5e560960098090437","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-001-engineering-definition-access/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:89dd5bbc3fa01ee2c8b18a90bddcb9ae5f06246adfcf2d911deec9395f45daf7","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-002-engineering-model-interpretation-and-identity-checks/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c0f370b5564e4e3a7fa5dc00a9276755929c35d0d9793e4c56552d785a5eb9e2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:aa5307eebf251ad71ac5200d76509e3666fad4fccd89384fc189364bd7a12e10","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-004-engineering-context-and-traceability/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:2469f00338b83e9a8a666c90c83cb079a52ea834241f9d0ec01c010066a50951","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-007-present-current-engineering-definition-and-applicable-rationale.json"},{"identity":"sha256:705977004fbc8037699b3af0210641e5ebef9b8404abe990e9e2bc55d2520e5f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-004-engineering-context-and-traceability/README.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered; Implementation and Verification are assessed separately."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"IF-002 uses the exact declaration and governing definitions bound to selected retained state, independent of the newest authoring profile.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Absent/conflicting declaration, unavailable definitions and unsupported/incompatible content return explicit gaps without fallback profile or silent migration.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Raw acquisition completeness and successful local interpretation remain distinct. Failed/partial content retains scoped findings and known identities but cannot yield a complete-model result.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Pure interpretation receives supplied content and cannot recursively retrieve or mutate source.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Governing entity, field, relationship, cardinality, identity, naming, lifecycle and validity definitions are available with the result or via exact state-bound references; missing context is an explicit interpretation limit.","number":5,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-010\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Interpret content under the selected state profile\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Interpretation and validation Module shall interpret supplied engineering content under the profile declared by its selected state, preserving subject and scope and reporting missing, unsupported, incompatible, or incomplete interpretation without silent migration or profile substitution.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Using today's rules on retained content can change its original meaning or produce false completeness.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Storage and authoring can rely on interpretation attributed to the actual selected state and declared profile.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-012 is a shared prerequisite for the IR-001 retrieval slice and retains its single parent under IR-005.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineering model authors and readers\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-003\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"Selected-state content requires interpretation before retention or retrieval is reported as understood.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-002 interpret_model_content.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Interpret supplied raw content, acquisition scope, and declaration with available authoritative profile definitions; avoid recursive interpreted retrieval.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"The shared interpretation responsibility used by the pilot; this AR does not complete all IR-005 architecture or define migration tooling.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"The same retained state is interpreted using its declared profile even if a newer profile exists.\",\n    \"Missing declarations, unavailable definitions, unsupported constructs, or incompatibilities produce explicit interpretation limits instead of a substitute current-profile interpretation.\",\n    \"Partial acquisition or failed interpretation cannot yield a complete-model result; the returned findings identify subject, state, profile, and inspected scope.\",\n    \"Interpretation does not modify the retained source or confer approval, conformance beyond its checked rules, or satisfaction.\",\n    \"Results identify the selected profile and provide its governing entity, field, relationship, cardinality, identity, naming, lifecycle, and validity definitions or resolvable state-bound references alongside the interpreted content; unavailable governing context is reported explicitly.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-003\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-012\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-ARCHITECTURE-PILOT\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-010\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-012 for the proposed MOD-003 responsibility and IR-001 scenario walkthrough. Acceptance criteria are intended observations, not executed verification or an approval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:3e22cfeeefcf0f6f0e2eb88c37865ac8babcaea6ab4909d3961fb23d6fd74044","path":"design/requirements/IR-005-keep-engineering-models-valid-and-consistently-interpreted/SR-012-interpret-model-states-using-their-identified-metamodel/AR-010-interpret-content-under-the-selected-state-profile.json"},"limitations":["Design only; no implementation, executed verification or satisfaction. Delivery unchanged.","Rust raw-capture/pure-check/candidate design needs adapter, mapping, capacity and platform qualification; adoption/persistence writers remain separate.","Semantic equivalence, mapping adequacy and consumer judgments require attributable assessment, not hashes/counts. No operational migration, workflow/profile adoption or transition authority."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-010","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 5 canonical AR-010 criteria; single-owner contribution where allocated.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:4917081e867bd98336b3da64e9208e06f5ad5c31b78754b209dfb334e5910c61","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-003-engineering-model-conformance/conformance-and-migration.md"},{"identity":"sha256:0ddf0e66a59db268afe1d3af8a671f4df82eac6cf63f8b6840b5b1b336c97eba","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-003-engineering-model-conformance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:3df0b81ddc90cf5abc6d4b8f8239e75a70a11e7ede9bc3de74ec1ce0e966f67f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-003-engineering-model-conformance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:08c55f688ee6e79439514ffbfc2160403f6bbc950cf6e36aac252eeeea6a4164","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7ed00afc1e82ff6fe2e273ccdc6c2d239a3d78ca21bd2db5e560960098090437","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-001-engineering-definition-access/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:89dd5bbc3fa01ee2c8b18a90bddcb9ae5f06246adfcf2d911deec9395f45daf7","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-002-engineering-model-interpretation-and-identity-checks/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:70a045bc5b7268265fafe19156f801ce0dd629b0305d7c948caf163cbf8f0368","path":"design/architecture/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:dcd46f9c5050b448c22730968f518884a887b023c250a534277737a6de5f9f86","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:264c5c99e22837edd8f3b4472a691c9a0c9c1fea05aa13adc7f1e0adc7eb8bab","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-001-engineering-model-storage/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:adcba795929cd96ff98cfffa6bc478e9972b15de44c9b12699e73e32e4436ee3","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-016-engineering-model-management/modules/MOD-004-engineering-context-and-traceability/allocation-and-impact.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9f6b3398a5cbbbc67e9cf98d2daf5d23978ac5174e8275983b0f39bab9af1481","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assurance-content.md"},{"identity":"sha256:62bcaa4c905652e7287c4419c4f7a3422016c6d4f84b2b0a2782b0087c1bce12","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assessment.md"},{"identity":"sha256:7339aa1fe37276f6f66e70aebd926c728add51dabd808d23f4769c147f845de5","path":"design/requirements/IR-005-keep-engineering-models-valid-and-consistently-interpreted/SR-012-interpret-model-states-using-their-identified-metamodel/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a327031b563b664a224cc8c9831322c3a4dbb19aea07a12418c4eec62d740b31","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-012-interpret-a-model-with-its-declared-metamodel.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; delivery unchanged."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-010 dispatch owns help before repository access where required and reports actual package/task availability, separating proposed browser/history operations.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Closed command parsing enforces duplicates, selector and configuration boundaries before dependent reads and emits safe fixed diagnostics.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"The successor selects schema-4 response projection from recognized dispatch even when request/backend admission fails; stored identities remain absent until observed.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Operational, maintenance, installation and diagnostics each retain their own version contract; coherent storage alone supplies revision identity.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Family-specific exit/result tables preserve true effects across human and structured forms, including uncertain commitment.","number":5,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Retired task/configuration handlers are rejected without discovery, rewriting configuration or routing to a predecessor backend.","number":6,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-011\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Admit supported commands under independent public contracts\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Command handling Module shall admit only explicitly selected supported command requests, apply their own help, selector, version, projection, and exit contracts, and reject unsupported or ambiguous input before the dependent access prohibited by that contract.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Ambiguous admission or a response version inferred from unvalidated input can direct a caller to the wrong operation or contract.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"A caller receives the selected command contract or its declared safe rejection before dependent work proceeds.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-040 requires predictable public admission and independent version domains; MOD-010 owns that public interpretation boundary.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineers and agents supplying explicit command requests\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-010 and its Interface consumers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A caller selects a public command, requests its help or package version, or supplies command flags, configuration, and request input.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The IF-004 public-command boundary, including dispatch to IF-003 operational records and the separately owned IF-006 installation contract.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Recognize the command and validate its closed selectors before dependent access, then preserve its specific request and response domain through dispatch and presentation.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Current public command families, their required early-error behavior, and the exact retired command/configuration set. Detailed installation mutations remain with Installation.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Recognized operation-specific help discloses that operation and common safety fields without repository access where required; package version/help identify the delivered supported interface rather than advertise withdrawn operations.\",\n    \"Unknown or duplicate flags, extra positionals, absent or contradictory required selectors, unsupported operations, and unknown configuration kinds reject at their declared boundary before filesystem or stdin access where required; invalid raw values are not echoed or replaced with invented selectors.\",\n    \"Recognized current operational tasks use their schema-4 response domain on early and late failures; an untrusted request or absent backend cannot select a predecessor response or invent stored identity.\",\n    \"Operational, maintenance, installation and diagnostic version domains remain independent. Return record/store revisions only when established from the relevant coherent state.\",\n    \"Each family preserves its declared human/JSON meaning and exit classes, including actual committed, failed, conflicting or uncertain effects.\",\n    \"Withdrawn command families, the removed query-shim interface, and the retired spec configuration kind acquire no fallback or advertised operational support; rejecting an override does not rewrite configuration or invoke discovery.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-010\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-040 / AR-011; MOD-010\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derive this draft lower-level obligation from the containing SR at the selected command or operational-record responsibility boundary. Allocation and acceptance criteria are design claims for review, not implementation, requirement approval, or satisfaction evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-02, CLI-SR-10, CLI-SR-17, CLI-SR-18, CLI-SR-27, CLI-SR-28, CLI-SR-30, CLI-SR-31, CLI-SR-32; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-14\",\n      \"basis\": \"Preserve the applicable current public and stored-record guarantees at this accountable boundary. The named source retains exact schemas, operation tables, classifications, limits, and historical adoption obligations; this allocation neither replaces those details nor accepts REM authoring JSON as operational records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-011\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconcile the complete existing allocation with the selected current v2/v4 contract, preserving independent admission, coherent state, explicit scope and actor judgment. Prior version-specific sources retain their historical meaning.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-040\",\n    \"FUNC-048\"\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:69ebec21dd9480253545e958d94c0fc31642df4025816225ac21c326cd50c0c0","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-040-preserve-explicit-command-admission-and-independent-interface-contracts/AR-011-admit-supported-commands-under-independent-public-contracts.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-011","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 6 canonical AR-011 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8cd48470112d1d1948365f950b015e92df117ac302661f26311de28f9b3e2b27","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-040-admit-explicit-requests-under-declared-command-contracts.json"},{"identity":"sha256:302fb1f00c393413ca968a5be04118d06d452a75f31da200675fbe56bcbf27dd","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-048-project-bounded-command-results-without-changing-meaning.json"},{"identity":"sha256:e304e00066c398fba035c8fee2830adce7ea0efa808610eb8612793a2017f253","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-040-preserve-explicit-command-admission-and-independent-interface-contracts/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"The project-associated SQLite metadata and v4 typed records distinguish record schema 4 from PRAGMA database schema and project identity.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Connection admission verifies supported project/schema and state before querying or mutating; unknown/corrupt state is unavailable rather than empty.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Ordinary store selection never discovers legacy directories or resumes their file journal; explicit qualified import is a different maintenance operation.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Maintenance stages complete typed validation, preserves source originals and attributable dispositions, and cannot promote imported historical judgments.","number":4,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-012\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Enforce the operational stored contract without historical reinterpretation\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Work records Module shall enforce the associated v4 SQLite store and supported schema on every ordinary entry path, with no legacy execution fallback or historical reinterpretation.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"An operational reader or recovery path can silently restore withdrawn stored-format support even when command admission rejects it.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Every persistence entry path enforces the same current stored boundary while historical content retains its original meaning.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-040 requires stored-contract rejection behind public dispatch; MOD-011 owns the records and recovery state that must enforce it.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineers and agents supplying explicit command requests\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-011 and its Interface consumers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"An ordinary task or query opens the associated project store, or explicit maintenance validates a replacement/import candidate.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The IF-003 operational-record boundary and the selected store, candidates, and recovery material it governs.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Check project association and database schema before current interpretation. Keep command, stored-record, database and backup versions independent; imports use only qualified source adapters.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Current v4 ordinary operation and explicit supported maintenance. Historical v3 originals are read only by the qualified source importer or repository historical validator, never an ordinary runtime fallback.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"New current records identify rigorloop-records-v4 and schema_version 4 in the associated project database; PRAGMA schema version and project metadata are separately validated.\",\n    \"Unknown or mismatched projects, unsupported database schemas and corrupt stores stop safely without initializing an empty substitute.\",\n    \"Legacy directory or journal residue cannot select an executable backend or trigger recovery; original records remain unchanged by ordinary access.\",\n    \"Qualified explicit import preserves selected source originals and dispositions; it does not promote earlier judgments or bypass ordinary current-record validation.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-011\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-040 / AR-012; MOD-011\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derive this draft lower-level obligation from the containing SR at the selected command or operational-record responsibility boundary. Allocation and acceptance criteria are design claims for review, not implementation, requirement approval, or satisfaction evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-10, CLI-SR-27, CLI-SR-28; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-01, RF-SR-06, RF-SR-09, RF-SR-12, RF-SR-14\",\n      \"basis\": \"Preserve the applicable current public and stored-record guarantees at this accountable boundary. The named source retains exact schemas, operation tables, classifications, limits, and historical adoption obligations; this allocation neither replaces those details nor accepts REM authoring JSON as operational records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-012\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconcile the complete existing allocation with the selected current v2/v4 contract, preserving independent admission, coherent state, explicit scope and actor judgment. Prior version-specific sources retain their historical meaning.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-044\",\n    \"FUNC-046\",\n    \"FUNC-047\"\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:062be55f60c780c095201a39be8120fdfac040f7c106d072801f5ddc63ae9f3d","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-040-preserve-explicit-command-admission-and-independent-interface-contracts/AR-012-enforce-the-operational-stored-contract-without-historical-reinterpretation.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-012","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 4 canonical AR-012 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:08ebb8b4277641cf25e8a4513093c053cc6ddc5740fdb9c6fb53660f8f27ede8","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-044-validate-registered-recording-candidates-and-preservation-rules.json"},{"identity":"sha256:baddee11461c8f1fed6430cc5e0709c002aa3b406905220d7118f4996e06165c","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-046-publish-fresh-record-candidates-as-coherent-transactions.json"},{"identity":"sha256:6f6c1c3dca121c812995f64590227d2aab3c7054d7c51394eaad27cd1a317331","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-047-recover-exact-interrupted-record-transactions.json"},{"identity":"sha256:e304e00066c398fba035c8fee2830adce7ea0efa808610eb8612793a2017f253","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-040-preserve-explicit-command-admission-and-independent-interface-contracts/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:aa678e0f86b857be5b57c30010f396852aa2755e7fc0d1f4572615b7b4d4dfc8","path":"schemas/rigorloop-records-v4.schema.json"},{"identity":"sha256:83a5da5a2332e5da113962fe2396642e09a5f0cf0040e50af2b70ec2823bb572","path":"schemas/targeted-recording-v2.schema.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"Closed explicit Change/item/context selectors own selection; workflow stage labels do not broaden queries.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"One stored authority supplies full selected content, support state and precise omission/absence metadata in derived views.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Typed reader errors distinguish missing, malformed and unavailable accounts from empty successful records or invented contract identity.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Declared selectors are deduplicated and bounded; the complete current-account index has no implicit cursor or retired paging fallback.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Complete-output and per-account admission bounds reject oversize without dropping rationale or unresolved issues.","number":5,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Capabilities inspects actual supported contracts/tasks and backend standing without legacy discovery or engineering authority selection.","number":6,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Ordinary reads change no engineering facts and choose no replacement; SQLite may resolve only its already determined journal outcome.","number":7,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-013\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Return exactly selected records and factual discovery context\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Command handling Module shall return the explicitly selected current operational information and factual capabilities with coherent scope and availability, without selecting authority or choosing maintenance recovery.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Even a valid snapshot becomes misleading if command selection adds inferred records, hides omissions, or presents unavailable content as an empty result.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"A caller can distinguish the requested recorded information from excluded, omitted, unavailable, or unobserved information.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-041 assigns meaning to explicit selection and discovery; MOD-010 owns those query rules and their public presentation.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineers and agents supplying explicit command requests\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-010 and its Interface consumers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A caller requests capabilities, Change context, or a selected Review or Verification.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-004 current query presentation using IF-003 coherent reads and availability facts.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Provide explicit scoped current-context and item queries plus project capability inspection through the current CLI, preserving coherent values and truthful limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Current operational query responsibility; no requirement to scan docs/changes, expose SQL, enumerate the database or preserve the predecessor query grammar.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Admit explicit Change/item queries and optional bounded context selectors; no stage label implicitly broadens selection.\",\n    \"Return full selected meaning and current support, with explicit absent/omitted distinctions; views are derived from one authority.\",\n    \"Unknown, unavailable or malformed content does not become an empty valid record or inferred contract.\",\n    \"Deduplicate and bound declared selectors according to the closed current query contract; no retired cursor/page interface is implied.\",\n    \"Oversized selected accounts fail explicitly rather than truncate rationale or hide unresolved issues.\",\n    \"Capabilities reports actual executable tasks, contract identity and backend standing without scanning legacy directories or choosing authority.\",\n    \"Read operations never author engineering state or choose replacement recovery; SQLite may recover its already determined transaction outcome.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Current selected task/query contract; predecessor filesystem discovery and field-projection interfaces are retired in the successor.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-010\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-041 / AR-013; MOD-010\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derive this draft lower-level obligation from the containing SR at the selected command or operational-record responsibility boundary. Allocation and acceptance criteria are design claims for review, not implementation, requirement approval, or satisfaction evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-01, CLI-SR-14, CLI-SR-21, CLI-SR-22, CLI-SR-23, CLI-SR-24, CLI-SR-28, CLI-SR-32; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-02, RF-SR-07\",\n      \"basis\": \"Preserve the applicable current public and stored-record guarantees at this accountable boundary. The named source retains exact schemas, operation tables, classifications, limits, and historical adoption obligations; this allocation neither replaces those details nor accepts REM authoring JSON as operational records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"MOD-010 current task/query contract; MOD-011 typed read boundary\",\n      \"basis\": \"Refines the existing inspection need to the selected successor task interface; no new IR or implementation approval.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-041\",\n    \"FUNC-042\",\n    \"FUNC-048\"\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:39cac611055b8763e6db96c8ea08583328f52e1d540e9b4b718d0f1b330a3683","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-041-return-coherent-explicitly-selected-engineering-records-and-subject-identities/AR-013-return-exactly-selected-records-and-factual-discovery-context.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-013","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 7 canonical AR-013 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:aeebb69c87ad3b4a58af3ea78b5440819747af148aa693fb7380ab38b64c4b02","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-041-inspect-project-capabilities-and-selected-current-context.json"},{"identity":"sha256:e68e25ece2077c38e01cd2a3f707d754b3787bc5acd067b400def1426bdd5d96","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-042-read-explicitly-selected-engineering-records.json"},{"identity":"sha256:302fb1f00c393413ca968a5be04118d06d452a75f31da200675fbe56bcbf27dd","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-048-project-bounded-command-results-without-changing-meaning.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3c2601dee21b1a7fe6e82bbfd1ed47a62d688a4113fc4592d21f993b7b62fe20","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-041-return-coherent-explicitly-selected-engineering-records-and-subject-identities/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"The associated read transaction captures typed values, contract metadata and revision from one snapshot.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Typed database rows and validated references define authority; unrelated physical files cannot enter by discovery.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Missing rows and lost registered payloads produce explicit diagnostic/availability gaps rather than successful evidence.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"SQLite snapshot reads and bounded contention return coherent facts or busy/unavailable; internal recovery cannot replay actor intent.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Absent, wrong-project, corrupt and unsupported stores return only known observations, without synthesizing a stored revision.","number":5,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"The read path performs no initialization, schema migration, compaction or engineering judgment mutation.","number":6,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-014\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Supply coherent registered snapshots with explicit availability\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Work records Module shall supply selected current values from the associated SQLite store with coherent revision and explicit absent, invalid, inaccessible, busy or recovery-needed standing, never a usable mixed snapshot.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A query cannot give trustworthy contract, revision, or completeness information when its supporting reads combine different states or conceal missing registered content.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"The command Module receives enough exact state and availability information to produce an honest selected read.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-041 depends on a coherent source of records; MOD-011 owns this state and IF-003 even though MOD-010 is primary for logical query behavior.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineers and agents supplying explicit command requests\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-011 and its Interface consumers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A selected current read is requested while the store may be absent, changing, interrupted or fenced for maintenance.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The IF-003 read boundary for the associated project SQLite database and explicitly referenced retained payloads.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Provide explicit scoped current-context and item queries plus project capability inspection through the current CLI, preserving coherent values and truthful limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Current operational query responsibility; no requirement to scan docs/changes, expose SQL, enumerate the database or preserve the predecessor query grammar.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Established contract, revision and values originate from one coherent associated SQLite snapshot.\",\n    \"Typed database relationships determine current record authority; extra physical files cannot enter the snapshot by discovery.\",\n    \"Missing selected rows and unavailable retained payloads remain explicit; they never become invented successful evidence.\",\n    \"Concurrent operations yield a coherent snapshot or explicit busy/unavailable result. SQLite-internal recovery does not replay decisions.\",\n    \"No stored revision or contract is invented for an absent, corrupt, mismatched or unsupported database.\",\n    \"Reads never initialize, migrate, compact payloads or change engineering judgments.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Current selected task/query contract; predecessor filesystem discovery and field-projection interfaces are retired in the successor.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-011\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-041 / AR-014; MOD-011\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derive this draft lower-level obligation from the containing SR at the selected command or operational-record responsibility boundary. Allocation and acceptance criteria are design claims for review, not implementation, requirement approval, or satisfaction evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-01, CLI-SR-04, CLI-SR-05, CLI-SR-14, CLI-SR-21, CLI-SR-22, CLI-SR-23; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-02, RF-SR-07\",\n      \"basis\": \"Preserve the applicable current public and stored-record guarantees at this accountable boundary. The named source retains exact schemas, operation tables, classifications, limits, and historical adoption obligations; this allocation neither replaces those details nor accepts REM authoring JSON as operational records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"MOD-010 current task/query contract; MOD-011 typed read boundary\",\n      \"basis\": \"Refines the existing inspection need to the selected successor task interface; no new IR or implementation approval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:93be579848c63a430c50793e27cb3da84a757398f43d41945c40a6a50a022676","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-041-return-coherent-explicitly-selected-engineering-records-and-subject-identities/AR-014-supply-coherent-registered-snapshots-with-explicit-availability.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-014","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 6 canonical AR-014 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:3c2601dee21b1a7fe6e82bbfd1ed47a62d688a4113fc4592d21f993b7b62fe20","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-041-return-coherent-explicitly-selected-engineering-records-and-subject-identities/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"Declared Subject selections and compared/reported/unknown basis modes identify exactly what was mechanically observed.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Contained regular-file and bounded-byte checks expose missing, unsafe, symlinked, unreadable or oversized subjects as gaps or safe rejection.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"The dependent task rechecks original comparisons before commit and rejects mismatch; unstable inspection cannot assert a coherent match.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Only the supplied subject set is acquired; no inferred dependency expansion or authority selection occurs.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Original assessed expectations remain unchanged. Corrected final observation reports late drift/unavailable comparison without rewriting history or claiming future external stability.","number":5,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-015\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Compare explicitly declared engineering subjects safely\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Work records Module shall compare explicitly declared contained engineering subjects with the supplied basis, report observed gaps, and never silently replace the actor’s expected or assessed subjects.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Refreshing caller expectations or conflating reported and observed basis can silently broaden an assessment.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Compared basis is factual, scope-limited and distinct from the attributed judgment.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-041 requires honest reported/compared basis for current decisions; MOD-011 supplies safe declared-read checks for tasks and review preparation.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineers and agents supplying explicit command requests\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-011 and its Interface consumers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A task supplies compared reads, or review preparation checks explicitly assessed subjects.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-003 declared-read admission and review preparation, presented through IF-004.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Inspect only admitted contained regular files with bounded observations and freshness checks; compare supplied expectations without executing content or converting observations to approval.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Declared compared basis and explicit absence only; no standalone subject command, full-content inspection mode, universal file hashing or Git requirement.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Compared observations identify the explicitly selected subjects and distinguish reported basis from mechanically checked basis.\",\n    \"Missing, unsafe, symlinked, unreadable or over-limit subjects produce explicit applicable gaps or safe rejection, never invented matching content.\",\n    \"Declared-read mismatch rejects a dependent mutation without partial state; observed changes during inspection cannot produce an asserted coherent match.\",\n    \"Only declared subjects are inspected; no dependency discovery or automatic authority selection broadens the scope.\",\n    \"Observations do not refresh supplied expectations or rewrite historical assessed subjects; external edits remain covered only at the defined observed checks.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-011\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-041 / AR-015; MOD-011\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derive this draft lower-level obligation from the containing SR at the selected command or operational-record responsibility boundary. Allocation and acceptance criteria are design claims for review, not implementation, requirement approval, or satisfaction evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-19, CLI-SR-04, CLI-SR-09\",\n      \"basis\": \"Preserve the applicable current public and stored-record guarantees at this accountable boundary. The named source retains exact schemas, operation tables, classifications, limits, and historical adoption obligations; this allocation neither replaces those details nor accepts REM authoring JSON as operational records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-015; MOD-011 declared reads and review preparation\",\n      \"basis\": \"Refines the existing SR-041 allocation to current compared-read support; retires predecessor full-content subject modes without weakening containment or attribution.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-043\"\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:302f427261aabad0c2b47017f3c5a71fa3e4aedae6c73a970dac8038c72fd041","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-041-return-coherent-explicitly-selected-engineering-records-and-subject-identities/AR-015-compare-explicitly-declared-engineering-subjects-safely.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-015","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 5 canonical AR-015 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:434f43bf113bed30acca0f4a0d1b2d5134b3d2a2c4ff36858b1b93ac27145901","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-043-compare-declared-engineering-subjects.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3c2601dee21b1a7fe6e82bbfd1ed47a62d688a4113fc4592d21f993b7b62fe20","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-041-return-coherent-explicitly-selected-engineering-records-and-subject-identities/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d679737e5385227ecd2100b394060797eeb399de2c2821791d96bf30c9488a04","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/test-design.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"Closed request/record shapes, encoding and duplicate checks precede typed candidate construction and publication.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Registry/body totality, kind, Change association and required applicability are validated; extra physical files cannot supply a typed record.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Complete-candidate reference checks enforce exact field-compatible same-Change targets and reject missing, ambiguous or wrong-kind references.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Deferred valid cycles and explicitly introduced related records resolve in the same complete candidate before commit.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Distinct Review/Verification shapes retain scope, basis, support and limits; adverse assessments need not fabricate success prerequisites.","number":5,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Preview, execution and staged maintenance all apply current candidate invariants, which confer no approval or execution permission.","number":6,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-016\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Validate complete candidates against the closed registered record contract\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Work records Module shall validate complete typed current candidates against closed shapes, identities, support and reference rules before publication, without inferring omitted judgments.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A candidate can appear readable while carrying unknown vocabulary, ambiguous identities, incomplete registration, or references that resolve differently for different consumers.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"All supported candidate entry paths obtain one structurally admissible final representation or a precise safe rejection.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-042 requires closed current-record validity; MOD-011 owns the complete candidate and shared validation responsibility.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineers and agents supplying explicit command requests\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-011 and its Interface consumers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"An ordinary task or staged maintenance candidate requires current-record validation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The shared IF-003 validation boundary for a coherent Change and its typed supporting accounts.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Reject malformed closed values before checking exact typed references, attribution and preservation against the complete candidate.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"The current v4 record shapes and dependency rules, separate from REM conformance and engineering adequacy.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Unknown fields or closed-vocabulary values, duplicate keys or identities, missing required values, invalid encodings or versions, mixed stores, body/dual assessment representations, and malformed current records reject before authoritative writes.\",\n    \"Each supporting record has matching kind and Change identity plus explicit applicability where its selected contract requires a reliance declaration. A physical registry is adapter-owned bookkeeping; an extra physical file contributes no authority.\",\n    \"Every typed reference resolves exactly one field-compatible object within the same complete candidate and declared identity namespace. Missing, ambiguous, wrong-kind, or cross-Change fallback targets reject.\",\n    \"Related typed references may resolve to entries explicitly introduced by the same task in its complete candidate; intermediate construction grants no workflow authority.\",\n    \"Review and Verification assessments preserve their explicit scope, governing basis, support and limitations; incomplete shapes reject, while missing success prerequisites do not prohibit a truthful adverse assessment.\",\n    \"Preview, execution and staged maintenance use the same current candidate invariants. Validation grants neither engineering approval nor external execution authority.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-011\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-042 / AR-016; MOD-011\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derive this draft lower-level obligation from the containing SR at the selected command or operational-record responsibility boundary. Allocation and acceptance criteria are design claims for review, not implementation, requirement approval, or satisfaction evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-02, CLI-SR-12, CLI-SR-15, CLI-SR-27; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-01, RF-SR-02, RF-SR-08, RF-SR-09, RF-SR-11\",\n      \"basis\": \"Preserve the applicable current public and stored-record guarantees at this accountable boundary. The named source retains exact schemas, operation tables, classifications, limits, and historical adoption obligations; this allocation neither replaces those details nor accepts REM authoring JSON as operational records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-CONTRACTS\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-016\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconcile the existing allocation with refined SR-042–044 and the explicit v4/v2 contract. Keep current-v3 byte and mutation guarantees version-scoped, preserve historical originals, and distinguish precommit recovery from committed outcome reporting. This target allocation is not runtime qualification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-016\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconcile the complete existing allocation with the selected current v2/v4 contract, preserving independent admission, coherent state, explicit scope and actor judgment. Prior version-specific sources retain their historical meaning.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-044\"\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:30a475c3fb3efa93871de6f8332fe83a30b595a0af9bb81bf305676922f53c26","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-042-validate-current-operational-candidates-without-inventing-decisions/AR-016-validate-complete-candidates-against-the-closed-registered-record-contract.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-016","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 6 canonical AR-016 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:08ebb8b4277641cf25e8a4513093c053cc6ddc5740fdb9c6fb53660f8f27ede8","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-044-validate-registered-recording-candidates-and-preservation-rules.json"},{"identity":"sha256:47d951f11efe0fe318382c04f401eec0d044537042aef6991c4172849fd817b6","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-042-validate-current-operational-candidates-without-inventing-decisions/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:aa678e0f86b857be5b57c30010f396852aa2755e7fc0d1f4572615b7b4d4dfc8","path":"schemas/rigorloop-records-v4.schema.json"},{"identity":"sha256:83a5da5a2332e5da113962fe2396642e09a5f0cf0040e50af2b70ec2823bb572","path":"schemas/targeted-recording-v2.schema.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"Typed construction and faithful projection preserve actor fields, ordered explanation arrays and multiline content without a second report authority.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Stable retained issue IDs survive omission; explicit attributed disposition plus dependency checks govern later compaction.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"A replacement clean assessment cannot erase open findings; disposed detail may be removed only through explicit safe compaction.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Current v4 issue accounts and original v3 blocker/Origin meaning remain version distinct; import preserves historical attribution and active reliance.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Adverse correction is admitted while new accepted bases/final success independently require current support; invalid references and stale expectations still reject.","number":5,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Recorded dependency checks expose reliance gaps but neither labels nor hashes establish independence, adequacy or unreported repository stability.","number":6,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-017\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Preserve actor decisions and distinct concern identity rules\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Work records Module shall preserve unresolved obligations and the attribution, scope and support of retained judgments while allowing explicit current-state replacement and dependency-safe compaction.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A shaped update can erase unresolved work or silently broaden a judgment.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Corrections remain possible with attributable current obligations and honest reliance gaps.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-042 separates structural validity from engineering judgment and preserves the facts needed for sound current decisions.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineers and agents supplying explicit command requests\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-011 and its Interface consumers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A candidate changes assessments, explanation values, findings, or blockers, or contains failed evidence, completed activity, or historical subject drift.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-003 validation against the coherent prior records and complete candidate for the same selected change.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Compare only the preservation invariants applicable to the declared operation, retaining supplied decisions and separating recorded assertions from current mechanical observations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Current actor-supplied scope, subjects, narrative, status, issue identity and assessment support; no exhaustive history or mandatory immutable-origin snapshots.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Actor-supplied status, subjects, applicability, provenance, explanation collection order and multiline meaning survive validation unchanged; neither a renderer nor validation creates another authoritative report.\",\n    \"Issue IDs remain stable while their accounts are retained. Omission never removes a finding; explicit disposition and dependency-free compaction follow the selected contract.\",\n    \"Assessment replacement preserves unresolved findings even when the new assessment is clean. V4 permits removal of disposed details only with explicit reason and no surviving reliance.\",\n    \"V3 retains immutable change-level blocker Origins. V4 uses attributable current issue accounts and dispositions without mandatory origin snapshots or complete history; no update silently rewrites a judgment still relied upon.\",\n    \"Adverse evidence, explicit invalidation and correction remain recordable. New accepted bases or successful final Verification require their declared support; invalid references and stale declared reads reject independently.\",\n    \"Actor labels, hashes and successful validation do not establish independence or engineering adequacy. Current support checks reconcile recorded dependencies, not unreported repository stability.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-011\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-042 / AR-017; MOD-011\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derive this draft lower-level obligation from the containing SR at the selected command or operational-record responsibility boundary. Allocation and acceptance criteria are design claims for review, not implementation, requirement approval, or satisfaction evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-07, CLI-SR-26; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-03, RF-SR-04, RF-SR-05, RF-SR-08, RF-SR-10, RF-SR-11, RF-SR-13\",\n      \"basis\": \"Preserve the applicable current public and stored-record guarantees at this accountable boundary. The named source retains exact schemas, operation tables, classifications, limits, and historical adoption obligations; this allocation neither replaces those details nor accepts REM authoring JSON as operational records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CURRENT-HANDOFF\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-017\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconcile current-state replacement, unresolved issue preservation and selective retention; retain version-specific v3 behavior until adoption.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-017\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconcile the complete existing allocation with the selected current v2/v4 contract, preserving independent admission, coherent state, explicit scope and actor judgment. Prior version-specific sources retain their historical meaning.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-044\"\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:1ea3f2c4b43573ba1f6ab13278c3eba0f060fe541869331503e8947534ae8366","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-042-validate-current-operational-candidates-without-inventing-decisions/AR-017-preserve-actor-decisions-and-distinct-concern-identity-rules.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-017","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 6 canonical AR-017 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:08ebb8b4277641cf25e8a4513093c053cc6ddc5740fdb9c6fb53660f8f27ede8","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-044-validate-registered-recording-candidates-and-preservation-rules.json"},{"identity":"sha256:47d951f11efe0fe318382c04f401eec0d044537042aef6991c4172849fd817b6","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-042-validate-current-operational-candidates-without-inventing-decisions/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:aa678e0f86b857be5b57c30010f396852aa2755e7fc0d1f4572615b7b4d4dfc8","path":"schemas/rigorloop-records-v4.schema.json"},{"identity":"sha256:83a5da5a2332e5da113962fe2396642e09a5f0cf0040e50af2b70ec2823bb572","path":"schemas/targeted-recording-v2.schema.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"The public task schema requires semantic intent, explicit scope and revision rather than inferring decisions from a role or stage.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Change creation names unused identity and explicit request/authority; it does not require fabricated prior requirement/design approval.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Bounded task variants separate evidence, assessment, issue disposition and completion while allowing their necessary coherent related facts.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Preview and execution share closed input semantics; only execution reacquires writer admission and fresh expectations.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"The successor has no arbitrary batch, advanced file replacement or SQL interface; skill callers use supported typed tasks.","number":5,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-018\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Admit explicit recording intent and nonwriting preview requests\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Command handling Module shall admit explicit bounded task intent and preserve its authority, scope and preview/execution distinction.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Defaulting actor decisions or changing scope can undermine explicit recording intent.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"The persistence boundary receives one unambiguous bounded semantic task with its declared basis and preview intent.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-043 requires explicit semantic inputs and equivalent nonwriting preview; MOD-010 owns their public admission and outcome meaning while MOD-011 constructs candidates.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineers and agents supplying explicit command requests\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-010 and its Interface consumers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A caller invokes a supported task mutation or its nonwriting preview.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-004 recording admission and the IF-003 construction, preview, and publication handoff.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the current v4 SQLite task and maintenance contract. Require explicit semantic task values, project/Change/item scope and current revision; missing or unknown input rejects without invented decisions.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocation preserves its existing parent SR and accountable Module. Prior v3 file-journal mechanisms are historical at 39be9c81; current maintenance remains separately explicit.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Require explicit semantic task values, project/Change/item scope and current revision; missing or unknown input rejects without invented decisions.\",\n    \"Creation selects an unused Change ID and explicit request/authority; it does not require or infer prior requirement/design approval.\",\n    \"Admit one bounded task with its related typed facts. Review assessment, evidence, issue disposition and completion remain distinct semantic operations.\",\n    \"Preview and execution use the same closed input definitions; preview makes no reservation and actual execution repeats freshness checks.\",\n    \"No legacy advanced replacement or arbitrary batch command survives. Skills use the public task contract without SQL or runtime-file reconstruction.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Current v4 SQLite realization; source observations do not establish engineering approval or passing implementation proof.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-010\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-043 / AR-018; MOD-010\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derive this draft lower-level obligation from the containing SR at the selected command or operational-record responsibility boundary. Allocation and acceptance criteria are design claims for review, not implementation, requirement approval, or satisfaction evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-03, CLI-SR-12, CLI-SR-15, CLI-SR-16, CLI-SR-25, CLI-SR-26; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-02, RF-SR-03\",\n      \"basis\": \"Preserve the applicable current public and stored-record guarantees at this accountable boundary. The named source retains exact schemas, operation tables, classifications, limits, and historical adoption obligations; this allocation neither replaces those details nor accepts REM authoring JSON as operational records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-CONTRACTS\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-018\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconcile the existing allocation with refined SR-042–044 and the explicit v4/v2 contract. Keep current-v3 byte and mutation guarantees version-scoped, preserve historical originals, and distinguish precommit recovery from committed outcome reporting. This target allocation is not runtime qualification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CURRENT-HANDOFF\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-018\",\n      \"basis\": \"Refine existing current-state responsibility and selective retention; observed runtime mappings remain version-scoped.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md; Work records (MOD-011) current transaction and maintenance contract\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconciles existing stakeholder need and allocation with SQLite ordinary recovery. No new need, approval, or executed result is inferred.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-040\",\n    \"FUNC-048\"\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:2634ca278cdefc262af88e13a9910dd9168a5d51854a68fbe01b153884c802cb","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-043-construct-lossless-updates-from-explicit-engineering-decisions/AR-018-admit-explicit-recording-intent-and-nonwriting-preview-requests.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-018","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 5 canonical AR-018 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8cd48470112d1d1948365f950b015e92df117ac302661f26311de28f9b3e2b27","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-040-admit-explicit-requests-under-declared-command-contracts.json"},{"identity":"sha256:302fb1f00c393413ca968a5be04118d06d452a75f31da200675fbe56bcbf27dd","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-048-project-bounded-command-results-without-changing-meaning.json"},{"identity":"sha256:9faf4546b6f931bfab3ee2ab3a25a6c54d6e149dd1ca696f60af47479f3dce20","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-043-construct-lossless-updates-from-explicit-engineering-decisions/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:aa678e0f86b857be5b57c30010f396852aa2755e7fc0d1f4572615b7b4d4dfc8","path":"schemas/rigorloop-records-v4.schema.json"},{"identity":"sha256:83a5da5a2332e5da113962fe2396642e09a5f0cf0040e50af2b70ec2823bb572","path":"schemas/targeted-recording-v2.schema.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-011 reconstructs the complete semantic candidate against its coherent transaction snapshot and checks every typed reference.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Targeted edits preserve omitted facts, unresolved concerns and supplied attribution/meaning; SQLite records do not promise old JSON whitespace.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Registry rows and related Change references publish in the same transaction without caller-managed manifests.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Conflicting assignments fail complete-candidate construction, leaving authoritative current facts unchanged.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Replacing comparable Evidence updates dependent support standing rather than retargeting the old assessment or Verify judgment.","number":5,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Account, selector and reserved issue-disposition bounds reject excessive growth before commit while retaining usable current concerns.","number":6,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Fresh candidate equality returns unchanged without revision advance; stale revision fails before equality can excuse it.","number":7,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Preview returns prospective facts and limits from a read snapshot, without persistence, approval or future reservation.","number":8,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-019\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Construct lossless complete candidates from explicit targeted edits\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Work records Module shall construct a complete current semantic candidate while preserving unresolved obligations and attributed assessment meaning.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Whole-file reconstruction, overlapping edits, or treating unavailable content as an empty file can silently overwrite neighboring decisions and invalidate the actor's bounded intent.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Only the requested semantic effects and necessary representation bookkeeping appear in the complete candidate, with no publication during construction.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-043 requires preservation of current decisions and unresolved obligations; MOD-011 owns typed candidate construction and dependency validation.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Engineers and agents supplying explicit command requests\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-011 and its Interface consumers\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"An admitted semantic task is constructed for preview or checked execution against one coherent current snapshot.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The IF-003 construction and validation boundary before the shared publication executor.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the current v4 SQLite task and maintenance contract. Construct one complete semantic candidate from explicit task intent against a coherent snapshot; reject malformed typed references before commitment.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocation preserves its existing parent SR and accountable Module. Prior v3 file-journal mechanisms are historical at 39be9c81; current maintenance remains separately explicit.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Construct one complete semantic candidate from explicit task intent against a coherent snapshot; reject malformed typed references before commitment.\",\n    \"Preserve omitted current facts, unresolved issues, assessor attribution and meaning; JSON file whitespace is not a SQLite semantic obligation.\",\n    \"Typed supporting records are linked atomically to their Change; callers need not maintain a filesystem registry.\",\n    \"Overlapping or inconsistent facts reject without partial semantic state.\",\n    \"Replacing comparable evidence does not silently renew dependent review or verification; current reliance gaps remain visible.\",\n    \"Bounded candidate and disposition reserve checks precede commitment; a too-large candidate does not strand ordinary issue disposition.\",\n    \"An identical complete candidate with fresh preconditions returns unchanged; a stale revision still conflicts.\",\n    \"Preview returns a candidate and limitations without claiming persistence, approval or reserved future access.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Current v4 SQLite realization; source observations do not establish engineering approval or passing implementation proof.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-011\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-043 / AR-019; MOD-011\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derive this draft lower-level obligation from the containing SR at the selected command or operational-record responsibility boundary. Allocation and acceptance criteria are design claims for review, not implementation, requirement approval, or satisfaction evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-03, CLI-SR-12, CLI-SR-13, CLI-SR-15, CLI-SR-16, CLI-SR-25, CLI-SR-26; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-02, RF-SR-03, RF-SR-04, RF-SR-08, RF-SR-10, RF-SR-11, RF-SR-13\",\n      \"basis\": \"Preserve the applicable current public and stored-record guarantees at this accountable boundary. The named source retains exact schemas, operation tables, classifications, limits, and historical adoption obligations; this allocation neither replaces those details nor accepts REM authoring JSON as operational records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-CONTRACTS\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-019\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconcile the existing allocation with refined SR-042–044 and the explicit v4/v2 contract. Keep current-v3 byte and mutation guarantees version-scoped, preserve historical originals, and distinguish precommit recovery from committed outcome reporting. This target allocation is not runtime qualification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CURRENT-HANDOFF\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-019\",\n      \"basis\": \"Refine existing current-state responsibility and selective retention; observed runtime mappings remain version-scoped.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md; Work records (MOD-011) current transaction and maintenance contract\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconciles existing stakeholder need and allocation with SQLite ordinary recovery. No new need, approval, or executed result is inferred.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-045\"\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:d8693af6d082d058dcb41281b3204a79b136ae7823bad0bdbc63c04be42c4e1c","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-043-construct-lossless-updates-from-explicit-engineering-decisions/AR-019-construct-lossless-complete-candidates-from-explicit-targeted-edits.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-019","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 8 canonical AR-019 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:727fa9085fec8f699361fc73b5e16db4a695ea168c91ffaffe5b5b56d5ee1b46","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-045-construct-lossless-candidates-from-explicit-record-edits.json"},{"identity":"sha256:9faf4546b6f931bfab3ee2ab3a25a6c54d6e149dd1ca696f60af47479f3dce20","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-043-construct-lossless-updates-from-explicit-engineering-decisions/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:aa678e0f86b857be5b57c30010f396852aa2755e7fc0d1f4572615b7b4d4dfc8","path":"schemas/rigorloop-records-v4.schema.json"},{"identity":"sha256:83a5da5a2332e5da113962fe2396642e09a5f0cf0040e50af2b70ec2823bb572","path":"schemas/targeted-recording-v2.schema.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"Stable project metadata and contained regular-file payload/read rules establish the selected local authority boundary.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"BEGIN IMMEDIATE serializes supported ordinary writers and compares the opaque incarnation/revision inside the transaction.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Only declared original expectations are compared; reported assertions retain actor attribution and cannot be silently refreshed.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"The lease/fence admission protocol excludes ordinary access throughout maintenance replacement and unresolved activation.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Old-revision retry conflicts despite equal desired facts; a fresh identical candidate returns unchanged without advancing revision.","number":5,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Unsupported schemas, wrong association, corruption or missing required storage primitives stop without empty initialization.","number":6,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-020\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Admit record publication only against a fresh contained basis\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Work records Module shall admit ordinary writes only against the associated project, current revision and declared basis under transaction and maintenance exclusion.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A validated candidate can become stale before publication, and an adapter-specific write path can bypass protection of other work.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"All supported writers make the same bounded freshness and target-safety decision against the state actually used for publication.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-044 requires conflict detection and safe retry before any candidate can become authoritative; preview or earlier structural success cannot reserve a state.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Actors recording explicit engineering decisions\",\n        \"Consumers of coherent operational records\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-011\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A supported creation or current-record task requests publication.\",\n        \"A candidate is repeated after preview, contention or a lost response.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-003 publication admission for one selected Change under SQLite writer exclusion and whole-store maintenance coordination.\",\n        \"Explicitly declared contained decision-basis subjects remain outside the write set.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the current v4 SQLite task and maintenance contract. Associate the stable project identity with the selected database and enforce safe contained paths for retained payloads and reads.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocation preserves its existing parent SR and accountable Module. Prior v3 file-journal mechanisms are historical at 39be9c81; current maintenance remains separately explicit.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Associate the stable project identity with the selected database and enforce safe contained paths for retained payloads and reads.\",\n    \"BEGIN IMMEDIATE excludes competing ordinary writers; expected opaque revision is checked in the transaction.\",\n    \"Declared compared subjects are checked without silently replacing caller expectations; reported basis remains actor-attributed.\",\n    \"Maintenance exclusion prevents ordinary operations from observing a partially activated replacement.\",\n    \"A stale lost-response retry conflicts even if its desired state equals current content; fresh no-op does not increment semantic revision.\",\n    \"Unknown schema, mismatched project, corrupt store or unavailable required filesystem primitives stop without creating an empty substitute.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Current v4 SQLite realization; source observations do not establish engineering approval or passing implementation proof.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-011\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-046\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-020\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-044 for the proposed MOD-011 responsibility. Allocates SR-044 acceptance criteria 1, 3, and 4, and the admission portions of criteria 2, 5, and 6 to FUNC-046. AR-021 owns durable publication and AR-022 applies the same protection boundary to explicit recovery. These criteria specify intended observations, not executed product evidence or an adoption of the REM authoring format by the CLI.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-03, CLI-SR-04, CLI-SR-08, CLI-SR-09, CLI-SR-12, CLI-SR-15, CLI-SR-16; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-08\",\n      \"basis\": \"Retains the named current CLI and Record Format obligations at this allocated responsibility boundary. Their detailed formats, supported versions, limits, and observed external-edit boundaries remain authoritative; no runtime behavior or public contract is changed by this draft.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md; Work records (MOD-011) current transaction and maintenance contract\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconciles existing stakeholder need and allocation with SQLite ordinary recovery. No new need, approval, or executed result is inferred.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:398973e3ee18f6d2e454dd5a9c1f967afd5132226041076a11121d0ab23cddb0","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-044-publish-record-updates-with-fresh-basis-and-coherent-durable-outcomes/AR-020-admit-record-publication-only-against-a-fresh-contained-basis.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-020","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 6 canonical AR-020 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:baddee11461c8f1fed6430cc5e0709c002aa3b406905220d7118f4996e06165c","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-046-publish-fresh-record-candidates-as-coherent-transactions.json"},{"identity":"sha256:9b9091d0f23302efc6f9b390dfcf37b0a0147d81654b1414be5b959ac9576719","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-044-publish-record-updates-with-fresh-basis-and-coherent-durable-outcomes/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d679737e5385227ecd2100b394060797eeb399de2c2821791d96bf30c9488a04","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/test-design.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"One verified SQLite transaction with foreign keys, WAL and FULL synchronization owns all related authoritative row changes.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Candidate integrity and pure fixed-profile receipt readiness, including the late-observation reserve, precede COMMIT.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Snapshot readers obtain coherent current rows; related facts do not become usable independently before transaction commitment.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Any failed precommit condition aborts the transaction; safely copied but unreferenced payloads remain nonauthoritative and require guarded cleanup.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"After interruption, engine recovery establishes the committed/uncommitted state; missing response is not evidence of rollback.","number":5,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Postcommit output/cleanup failure preserves known commitment or honest uncertainty, and late source observations cannot alter the supplied judgment.","number":6,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-021\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Publish exact record candidates as coherent durable transactions\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Work records Module shall publish complete operational updates atomically and report durable, failed or uncertain outcomes truthfully.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Publishing related facts separately or reporting success before commitment can expose intermediate state.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Saved identifies a complete durable update; failed or uncertain responses remain truthful and current inspection establishes the actual state.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-044 ties success to the complete durable semantic update and checked basis, not progress through individual writes.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Actors publishing related recorded decisions\",\n        \"Concurrent supported readers\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-011\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A freshness-checked semantic candidate is ready for atomic publication.\",\n        \"Publication is interrupted or a declared basis changes at a required commitment check.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-003 and the associated SQLite transaction; staged retained payloads use the separately defined containment and publication safeguards.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the current v4 SQLite task and maintenance contract. Use one SQLite transaction for the complete semantic update with foreign keys, WAL and full synchronization; no parallel file record journal is required.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocation preserves its existing parent SR and accountable Module. Prior v3 file-journal mechanisms are historical at 39be9c81; current maintenance remains separately explicit.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Use one SQLite transaction for the complete semantic update with foreign keys, WAL and full synchronization; no parallel file record journal is required.\",\n    \"Prepare a fitting result and validate complete candidate constraints before COMMIT.\",\n    \"Readers observe a coherent snapshot of authoritative current rows; related facts never appear as usable partial state.\",\n    \"On precommit failure roll back the task while preserving other committed work; unused staged payloads remain nonauthoritative until explicitly cleaned.\",\n    \"After interruption let SQLite recover the already determined committed/uncommitted outcome. Lost output alone cannot establish rollback.\",\n    \"Postcommit output or cleanup failure reports established committed or unknown status honestly; it does not change the engineering judgment.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Current v4 SQLite realization; source observations do not establish engineering approval or passing implementation proof.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-011\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-046\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-021\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-044 for the proposed MOD-011 responsibility. Allocates the commitment, coherent-read, read-basis recheck, and prepared-recovery contributions to all SR-044 publication paths through FUNC-046 and IF-003. AR-020 supplies safe admission and AR-022 defines explicit recovery. These criteria specify intended observations, not executed product evidence or an adoption of the REM authoring format by the CLI.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-04, CLI-SR-05, CLI-SR-06, CLI-SR-09, CLI-SR-12, CLI-SR-15; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-08\",\n      \"basis\": \"Retains the named current CLI and Record Format obligations at this allocated responsibility boundary. Their detailed formats, supported versions, limits, and observed external-edit boundaries remain authoritative; no runtime behavior or public contract is changed by this draft.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-CONTRACTS\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-021\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconcile the existing allocation with refined SR-042–044 and the explicit v4/v2 contract. Keep current-v3 byte and mutation guarantees version-scoped, preserve historical originals, and distinguish precommit recovery from committed outcome reporting. This target allocation is not runtime qualification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md; Work records (MOD-011) current transaction and maintenance contract\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconciles existing stakeholder need and allocation with SQLite ordinary recovery. No new need, approval, or executed result is inferred.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:d7ebbb30ecd1380277e398fff9081c4c506fb6715657acff2e03688e04437c64","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-044-publish-record-updates-with-fresh-basis-and-coherent-durable-outcomes/AR-021-publish-exact-record-candidates-as-coherent-durable-transactions.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-021","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 6 canonical AR-021 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:baddee11461c8f1fed6430cc5e0709c002aa3b406905220d7118f4996e06165c","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-046-publish-fresh-record-candidates-as-coherent-transactions.json"},{"identity":"sha256:9b9091d0f23302efc6f9b390dfcf37b0a0147d81654b1414be5b959ac9576719","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-044-publish-record-updates-with-fresh-basis-and-coherent-durable-outcomes/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d679737e5385227ecd2100b394060797eeb399de2c2821791d96bf30c9488a04","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/test-design.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"Ordinary recovery opens only supported associated storage and stops safely for corrupt or unsupported data.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"SQLite resolves the recorded transaction outcome; no actor task is replayed to manufacture it.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"A fresh scoped snapshot returns only established facts/revision and limitations, never recovery approval.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Confirmed commitment survives response loss; uncertainty requires inspection rather than undoing or assuming success.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Repeated inspection has no duplicate semantic effect and preserves unavailable/unknown distinctions.","number":5,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Explicit maintenance recovery uses the fence, exact operation/observation, staged candidate and verified prior units under separate finish/rollback rules.","number":6,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-022\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Recover only exact verified operational record transactions\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Work records Module shall establish ordinary transaction outcomes through supported storage recovery without guessing, semantic replay or rollback of committed work.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Lost output or interrupted writes can leave a caller uncertain whether its decision was committed.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"A coherent current state or explicit safe unavailability allows a fresh decision without replaying old semantic intent.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-045 requires establishing the already determined storage outcome without selecting a new engineering effect or rolling back committed work.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Actors resolving an interrupted recorded update\",\n        \"Consumers relying on acknowledged saved results\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-011\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"An ordinary command opens the associated supported SQLite store after interruption.\",\n        \"The storage engine cannot establish a coherent outcome or maintenance has fenced the store.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-003 ordinary current-state reads and transactions backed by SQLite WAL recovery.\",\n        \"Explicit replacement resume remains a separate maintenance operation with preserved prior and staged units.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the current v4 SQLite task and maintenance contract. Open only an associated supported database; corruption or unsupported state yields explicit unavailability without guessed repair.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocation preserves its existing parent SR and accountable Module. Prior v3 file-journal mechanisms are historical at 39be9c81; current maintenance remains separately explicit.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Open only an associated supported database; corruption or unsupported state yields explicit unavailability without guessed repair.\",\n    \"Storage-engine recovery establishes the already determined ordinary transaction outcome without replaying actor decisions.\",\n    \"Current inspection returns a coherent committed/prior snapshot and opaque revision when established, not a synthetic recovery approval.\",\n    \"Committed work cannot be rolled back to repair an absent response; uncommitted work cannot become success by retry inference.\",\n    \"Repeated inspection after interruption has no duplicate semantic effects; uncertain outcome remains explicitly uncertain.\",\n    \"Explicit staged store restoration/import recovery belongs to the maintenance contract, with fence, observed state, exact candidate and preserved prior units.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Current v4 SQLite realization; source observations do not establish engineering approval or passing implementation proof.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-011\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-047\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-022\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-045 for the proposed MOD-011 responsibility. Allocates SR-045 exact recovery, foreign-content preservation, acknowledged-commit limits, interruption, and retirement outcomes to FUNC-047. AR-023 owns explicit public selection and non-recovery command dispatch. These criteria specify intended observations, not executed product evidence or an adoption of the REM authoring format by the CLI.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-05, CLI-SR-06, CLI-SR-09, CLI-SR-10, CLI-SR-26, CLI-SR-27, CLI-SR-28; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-04, RF-SR-06, RF-SR-08, RF-SR-12, RF-SR-14\",\n      \"basis\": \"Retains the named current CLI and Record Format obligations at this allocated responsibility boundary. Their detailed formats, supported versions, limits, and observed external-edit boundaries remain authoritative; no runtime behavior or public contract is changed by this draft.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md; Work records (MOD-011) current transaction and maintenance contract\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconciles existing stakeholder need and allocation with SQLite ordinary recovery. No new need, approval, or executed result is inferred.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:fe01a896ef0ad18a8e6c0cda9325115f2c54a7ba1ee8d4060bee9266b717d6e0","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-045-recover-interrupted-record-transactions-without-guessing-or-replaying-decisions/AR-022-recover-only-exact-verified-operational-record-transactions.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-022","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 6 canonical AR-022 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:6f6c1c3dca121c812995f64590227d2aab3c7054d7c51394eaad27cd1a317331","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-047-recover-exact-interrupted-record-transactions.json"},{"identity":"sha256:0081301c4178d94946ea6ed316d9bdffeb4bb429934d6d8fcc35df17598abc0d","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-045-recover-interrupted-record-transactions-without-guessing-or-replaying-decisions/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d679737e5385227ecd2100b394060797eeb399de2c2821791d96bf30c9488a04","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/test-design.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"The caller resumes an interrupted ordinary update through normal scoped inspection, not a transaction-replay public command.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Ordinary reads may trigger only storage-internal recovery; import and replacement remain explicit maintenance choices.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"MOD-010 preserves selected project/Change and reports current observations without resubmitting failed intent or refreshing stale expectations.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Known committed/prior state and uncertainty are faithfully projected without equating storage recovery to engineering approval.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Explicit maintenance continuation names supported task, operation and fresh observation; it cannot auto-resubmit or invoke a legacy handler.","number":5,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-023\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Require explicit recovery selection and preserve its actual outcome\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Command handling Module shall distinguish ordinary interruption inspection from explicitly selected maintenance recovery and preserve actual outcome limits.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A command could silently replay uncertain work or choose a replacement state when only inspection was requested.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Ordinary inspection establishes current state; only explicit maintenance resume can finish or permissibly roll back a staged replacement.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-045 separates ordinary storage recovery from actor-authorized store replacement and requires truthful outcome limits at the public boundary.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Actors choosing how to resolve interrupted work\",\n        \"Consumers of command and recovery results\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-010\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"An ordinary command follows interruption, or a caller explicitly requests supported maintenance resume.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-004 query/task admission and reporting using IF-003 inspect_records or the selected maintenance operation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the current v4 SQLite task and maintenance contract. Admit a normal scoped inspection after an interrupted ordinary update; no public record-transaction completion/restore command is exposed.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocation preserves its existing parent SR and accountable Module. Prior v3 file-journal mechanisms are historical at 39be9c81; current maintenance remains separately explicit.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Admit a normal scoped inspection after an interrupted ordinary update; no public record-transaction completion/restore command is exposed.\",\n    \"Ordinary reads may trigger internal SQLite recovery but never choose a new engineering effect, import history or activate a replacement.\",\n    \"Preserve the supplied project/Change selection and report actual established state; do not replay the failed task or refresh stale writes.\",\n    \"Report truthful committed/prior/unknown standing through the command result without converting storage outcome into approval.\",\n    \"Maintenance finish or rollback requires an explicit supported task, operation identity and fresh recovery observation; no automatic resubmission or legacy handler.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Current v4 SQLite realization; source observations do not establish engineering approval or passing implementation proof.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-010\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-040\",\n    \"FUNC-042\",\n    \"FUNC-048\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-023\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-045 for the proposed MOD-010 responsibility. Allocates the command-side portion of SR-045, especially criterion 5 and explicit action/reporting across criteria 1 through 4. MOD-011 remains the sole owner of FUNC-047 and actual transaction recovery through AR-022. These criteria specify intended observations, not executed product evidence or an adoption of the REM authoring format by the CLI.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-05, CLI-SR-06, CLI-SR-09, CLI-SR-10, CLI-SR-11, CLI-SR-27, CLI-SR-28; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-06, RF-SR-12, RF-SR-14\",\n      \"basis\": \"Retains the named current CLI and Record Format obligations at this allocated responsibility boundary. Their detailed formats, supported versions, limits, and observed external-edit boundaries remain authoritative; no runtime behavior or public contract is changed by this draft.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md; Work records (MOD-011) current transaction and maintenance contract\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconciles existing stakeholder need and allocation with SQLite ordinary recovery. No new need, approval, or executed result is inferred.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:4b57b7d2bbcbddaadfe2bc47a200ee8834688979b869bb27fa0922e555599b00","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-045-recover-interrupted-record-transactions-without-guessing-or-replaying-decisions/AR-023-require-explicit-recovery-selection-and-preserve-its-actual-outcome.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-023","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 5 canonical AR-023 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8cd48470112d1d1948365f950b015e92df117ac302661f26311de28f9b3e2b27","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-040-admit-explicit-requests-under-declared-command-contracts.json"},{"identity":"sha256:e68e25ece2077c38e01cd2a3f707d754b3787bc5acd067b400def1426bdd5d96","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-042-read-explicitly-selected-engineering-records.json"},{"identity":"sha256:302fb1f00c393413ca968a5be04118d06d452a75f31da200675fbe56bcbf27dd","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-048-project-bounded-command-results-without-changing-meaning.json"},{"identity":"sha256:0081301c4178d94946ea6ed316d9bdffeb4bb429934d6d8fcc35df17598abc0d","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-045-recover-interrupted-record-transactions-without-guessing-or-replaying-decisions/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d679737e5385227ecd2100b394060797eeb399de2c2821791d96bf30c9488a04","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/test-design.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"Fixed family outcome tables preserve saved/unchanged/preview/conflict and recovery meanings, only known identities, separate observations/errors and persistence-only claims.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"The shared semantic projection preserves decoded narrative, array order, absence, scope and omission fields in text and JSON without interpreting literal escape text.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Selected reads encode completely within the bound or fail safely before output; mutations instead reserve mandatory receipts and omit optional details explicitly.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Stored Review/Verification values and payload availability supply the projection; no synthesized rationale or approval fills a gap.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"A bounded complete selector index exposes omitted context and supports smaller explicit reads without hidden pages.","number":5,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Compared scope and gaps are explicit; reported assertions and unsafe/unreadable material never become matching observations.","number":6,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Concise/detailed generic results preserve effects, exit and safe continuation independently of logs; dedicated operational/maintenance contracts and privacy rules remain separate.","number":7,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-024\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Present faithful bounded command outcomes and selected explanations\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Command handling Module shall present bounded complete selected content and actual effects under the owning result contract without changing meaning, scope, availability or semantic exit.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Formatting and summary logic can truncate explanation, conflate missing information with a favorable result, or hide drift behind unchanged record revision.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"The caller understands current selected content, explicit gaps and actual effects without a second authoritative rendering.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-046 requires truthful equivalent result meaning while keeping persistence and retrieval separate from engineering judgment.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"People reading recorded explanations\",\n        \"Agents consuming structured command outcomes\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-010\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"A current query, task, preview, maintenance, installation or diagnostic request returns an outcome.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-004 result encoding using typed IF-003 facts for operational work; other result domains retain their own contracts.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Serialize bounded complete results from coherent current facts before emission; reject oversized reads and preserve committed truth after output failure.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Current task receipts, selected context/accounts and independent installation/diagnostic formats; no diagnostic-page protocol.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Preserve saved, unchanged, valid preview, ok, rejected, conflict, busy, recovery-needed, and generic outcomes in their own operation/version/exit domains. Retain only independently available identities; distinguish observations from errors and limit a recording claim to persistence, never approval or satisfaction.\",\n    \"Text and JSON return equivalent selected fields, order, decoded multiline narrative, indentation, Unicode, literal backslash sequences, state, scope, optional absence, and omission metadata. Do not interpret literal escape text, synthesize a second explanation, or omit a required field merely for concise presentation.\",\n    \"A selected read that cannot fit the admitted complete-output bound fails before emitting partial content. Return the safe limit outcome and available selection/budget guidance; optional mutation details follow the guaranteed receipt rule instead of turning a completed save into rejection.\",\n    \"Selected Review and Verification content preserves scope, support, optional absence and unavailable payload distinctions. No projection invents rationale or approval.\",\n    \"Context uses a bounded complete selector index with explicit selection omissions, rather than hidden pagination or exhaustive database output.\",\n    \"Compared observations disclose the actual checked scope and gaps; reported assertions are not presented as mechanical comparison, and unsafe/unreadable subjects are not matching absence.\",\n    \"Generic concise and detailed projections retain the same mutations, semantic exit, and facts needed for safe continuation without log lookup. Preserve operational and maintenance result contracts separately; safe diagnostics never echo arbitrary payloads, invalid raw selectors, or secrets.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-010\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-042\",\n    \"FUNC-048\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-024\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-046 for the proposed MOD-010 responsibility. Allocates SR-046 criteria 1, 2, 4, 5, and 6 to MOD-010 result selection and projection. AR-025 and AR-026 compose the separate guaranteed prepublication-receipt obligation; MOD-011 supplies actual storage and observed-basis facts through IF-003. These criteria specify intended observations, not executed product evidence or an adoption of the REM authoring format by the CLI.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-07, CLI-SR-11, CLI-SR-14, CLI-SR-17, CLI-SR-20, CLI-SR-21, CLI-SR-22, CLI-SR-24, CLI-SR-26, CLI-SR-27, CLI-SR-29, CLI-SR-30; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-03, RF-SR-07, RF-SR-10\",\n      \"basis\": \"Retains the named current CLI and Record Format obligations at this allocated responsibility boundary. Their detailed formats, supported versions, limits, and observed external-edit boundaries remain authoritative; no runtime behavior or public contract is changed by this draft.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-024\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconcile current bounded task receipts with complete selected results and truthful commit outcomes; predecessor cursor/ordinary-journal protocols remain historical.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:9bcb6bea2f0d73fc1b0bd8c30afdba0200f2bac04cc14b8e2939a36576e3cb2f","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-046-return-bounded-faithful-command-outcomes-and-selected-explanations/AR-024-present-faithful-bounded-command-outcomes-and-selected-explanations.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-024","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 7 canonical AR-024 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:e68e25ece2077c38e01cd2a3f707d754b3787bc5acd067b400def1426bdd5d96","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-042-read-explicitly-selected-engineering-records.json"},{"identity":"sha256:302fb1f00c393413ca968a5be04118d06d452a75f31da200675fbe56bcbf27dd","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-048-project-bounded-command-results-without-changing-meaning.json"},{"identity":"sha256:9edd655f49189ce4a3f5c07c6e2e86777637cbcc101592f300f2882f527302fd","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-046-return-bounded-faithful-command-outcomes-and-selected-explanations/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d679737e5385227ecd2100b394060797eeb399de2c2821791d96bf30c9488a04","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/test-design.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-011 supplies the current guarded candidate facts to a pure MOD-010-owned fixed-profile codec; changed candidate/profile requires fresh readiness, and preview grants no reservation.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Mandatory receipt bounds reserve common identity/revision/effects and a bounded observation summary independently of diagnostic count, including the final source check.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Deterministic changed-record summaries include count/omitted metadata; full accounts remain accessible through explicit reads rather than diagnostic continuation.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"The exact fixed-profile result is prepared before publication with no storage capability exposed to the codec; serialization failure stops precommit instead of becoming diagnostic overflow policy.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Final projection follows actual persistence outcome; late stdout/format failure retains committed status and directs fresh inspection, never false storage rejection.","number":5,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-025\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Prepare fitting publication receipts before authoritative mutation\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Command handling Module shall serialize the required public storage receipt for an admitted publication before authoritative mutation, using exact candidate facts and the selected operation and format, with mandatory output guaranteed to fit independently of optional diagnostic volume.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Rendering after publication can discover an avoidable overflow or misreport a successful write as a rejected operation.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Every admissible correction has a fitting mandatory receipt before commitment, and optional detail cannot change the truth of the eventual storage outcome.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-046 makes bounded receipt preparation a prerequisite of publication while forbidding diagnostic volume from becoming a new eligibility rule for a structurally valid correction.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Actors submitting corrections to diagnostic-heavy stores\",\n        \"Consumers of mutation receipts\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-010\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"An admitted candidate is prepared for publication in a selected command-family format.\",\n        \"Optional diagnostics or mechanical details exceed the space remaining beyond mandatory output.\",\n        \"Output delivery fails after an actual committed save.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"MOD-010 public rendering responsibility at IF-004.\",\n        \"Candidate facts and publication readiness exchanged with MOD-011 through IF-003.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Use exact supplied candidate/revision/target and bounded observation facts to serialize the family-specific mandatory receipt before publication. Bind readiness to that same candidate, operation, and format; summarize or explicitly omit optional detail rather than rejecting an admissible correction.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"The source-defined mandatory receipt reserve and total mutation limits apply to their owning public families. MOD-010 owns the output contract and serialization; MOD-011 owns actual candidate and commitment facts. No new transport token, callback, wire schema, or persistent receipt ledger is required.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Under guarded execution, construct and validate the exact current task candidate and supply its revision, affected identities and observations to the MOD-010 pure receipt encoder before commit. A changed candidate/profile requires new preparation; preview grants no later write reservation.\",\n    \"For every structurally admissible mutation, mandatory receipt content fits its source-defined reserved bound independently of the number of admitted diagnostic occurrences. A primary receipt carries the required common fields, identity/revision, changed targets, and at most the bounded observation summary; diagnostic bodies and optional effect expansion do not enter that guarantee.\",\n    \"Bound changed-item summaries with explicit omission counts; retain mandatory safe-continuation facts. Complete selected current accounts remain available through supported reads; no diagnostic cursor is required.\",\n    \"Provide persistence only readiness established for the exact selected operation/candidate/format before authoritative publication. Unexpected serialization failure stops before writing as an implementation failure, not a supported diagnostic-overflow rejection policy.\",\n    \"Project the actual terminal storage result returned by persistence. Once saved or unchanged is established, later renderer or stdout-delivery failure cannot be reported as a storage rejection; retain the source transport/lost-response boundary and require normal fresh-state handling for a later retry.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-010\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-048\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-025\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-046 for the proposed MOD-010 responsibility. Allocates SR-046 criterion 3 and the rendering contribution to criteria 1, 2, and 6 solely to MOD-010/FUNC-048. AR-026 supplies exact storage facts, honors bound readiness before mutation, and returns the actual commitment disposition. These criteria specify intended observations, not executed product evidence or an adoption of the REM authoring format by the CLI.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-11, CLI-SR-17, CLI-SR-20, CLI-SR-30\",\n      \"basis\": \"Retains the named current CLI and Record Format obligations at this allocated responsibility boundary. Their detailed formats, supported versions, limits, and observed external-edit boundaries remain authoritative; no runtime behavior or public contract is changed by this draft.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-025\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconcile current bounded task receipts with complete selected results and truthful commit outcomes; predecessor cursor/ordinary-journal protocols remain historical.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:c3c216543b9e151ca82f6d6140dc3a490e875e00dcc83dc87a4b176e69912776","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-046-return-bounded-faithful-command-outcomes-and-selected-explanations/AR-025-prepare-fitting-publication-receipts-before-authoritative-mutation.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-025","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 5 canonical AR-025 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:302fb1f00c393413ca968a5be04118d06d452a75f31da200675fbe56bcbf27dd","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-048-project-bounded-command-results-without-changing-meaning.json"},{"identity":"sha256:9edd655f49189ce4a3f5c07c6e2e86777637cbcc101592f300f2882f527302fd","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-046-return-bounded-faithful-command-outcomes-and-selected-explanations/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d679737e5385227ecd2100b394060797eeb399de2c2821791d96bf30c9488a04","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/test-design.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"Under writer admission MOD-011 constructs and validates the exact current candidate and prepared receipt; maintenance separately binds staged state and recovery expectations.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Declared compared observations and reported basis retain distinct scope and explicit missing/unsafe gaps without global stability claims.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Receipt readiness binds operation/candidate/profile and reserved late-observation form; changed facts require re-preparation, while optional diagnostic volume cannot invalidate a sound correction.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Only durable complete publication yields saved; no-op requires fresh checks, and conflict/busy/unavailable/uncertain outcomes carry only actually known identities and effects.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Confirmed commit survives output failure and postcommit basis drift; true or unknown commitment remains explicit and subsequent action requires fresh inspection rather than rollback.","number":5,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-026\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Bind publication to prepared receipts and report actual storage effects\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Work record storage Module shall supply exact candidate and observed-state facts for receipt preparation, publish only with applicable prepublication readiness for those facts, and return the actual known storage outcome without allowing reporting limitations to misrepresent commitment.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A command renderer cannot guarantee truthful bounded output if persistence publishes a different candidate or hides the resulting transaction state.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"The prepared public receipt and actual storage operation refer to the same subject, and the command receives reliable facts for saved, unchanged, conflict, interruption, or recovery outcomes.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-046 receipt safety requires cooperation at the mutation boundary while keeping output-contract ownership in MOD-010 and byte/commitment ownership in MOD-011.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Command adapters preparing safe storage receipts\",\n        \"Actors relying on truthful transaction outcomes\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-011\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"An ordinary task reaches the transaction commit boundary, or a separately selected maintenance operation establishes its actual outcome.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"IF-003 typed outcomes and the qualified database or maintenance boundary.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Construct current facts under exclusion and call the fixed pure receipt encoder before commitment. Return known committed, unchanged, failed or uncertain state; never replay semantics for cleaner output.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"MOD-011 supplies storage and observed-basis facts and enforces the prepublication condition; MOD-010 retains FUNC-048 and the public output limits/serialization. No extra rendering Function, mandatory callback, new public protocol, or inferred approval is introduced.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Under supported exclusion, read the coherent current state, check supplied revision/reads and construct the typed candidate. Establish receipt readiness for those same candidate facts before committing. Maintenance separately validates selected staged state and observed recovery expectations; ordinary SQLite recovery does not replay tasks.\",\n    \"Reported and compared basis remain distinguishable, and observations derive from the selected current checked scope. Missing or unsafe subjects remain explicit; no global repository-stability claim is inferred.\",\n    \"Before authoritative publication, ensure the mandatory receipt readiness applies to the exact operation, candidate, format, and required facts supplied for that attempt. A changed candidate or stale basis cannot reuse earlier readiness; known nonmatching or unavailable readiness stops before publication while preserving the source guarantee that diagnostic volume alone cannot make an admissible correction unrecordable.\",\n    \"Return saved only for the actual durably committed candidate, unchanged only after its current preconditions pass, and conflict, busy, failed, or recovery-needed when those are the actual known outcomes. Supply available identities and transaction context without inventing a coherent snapshot or presenting a partially published changed list as a saved result.\",\n    \"After commit, reporting failure cannot turn saved into rejected or roll back committed work. Return committed=true where established, unknown where necessary, and require current inspection before a fresh actor decision.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-011\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-046\",\n    \"FUNC-047\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-026\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-046 for the proposed MOD-011 responsibility. Allocates the persistence contribution to SR-046 criteria 1, 3, and 4. AR-025 remains the sole public receipt preparation owner; AR-021 and AR-022 establish the underlying committed and recovered facts consumed here. These criteria specify intended observations, not executed product evidence or an adoption of the REM authoring format by the CLI.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-05, CLI-SR-06, CLI-SR-08, CLI-SR-11, CLI-SR-20, CLI-SR-26; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md#RF-SR-08\",\n      \"basis\": \"Retains the named current CLI and Record Format obligations at this allocated responsibility boundary. Their detailed formats, supported versions, limits, and observed external-edit boundaries remain authoritative; no runtime behavior or public contract is changed by this draft.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-SQLITE-ADOPTION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-026\",\n      \"basis\": \"Reconcile current bounded task receipts with complete selected results and truthful commit outcomes; predecessor cursor/ordinary-journal protocols remain historical.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:eafbcddc06dfd0c094310a3d9416b7bf5f8d796e95290faf73d0612a8c68f7d2","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-046-return-bounded-faithful-command-outcomes-and-selected-explanations/AR-026-bind-publication-to-prepared-receipts-and-report-actual-storage-effects.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-026","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 5 canonical AR-026 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:baddee11461c8f1fed6430cc5e0709c002aa3b406905220d7118f4996e06165c","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-046-publish-fresh-record-candidates-as-coherent-transactions.json"},{"identity":"sha256:6f6c1c3dca121c812995f64590227d2aab3c7054d7c51394eaad27cd1a317331","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-047-recover-exact-interrupted-record-transactions.json"},{"identity":"sha256:9edd655f49189ce4a3f5c07c6e2e86777637cbcc101592f300f2882f527302fd","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-046-return-bounded-faithful-command-outcomes-and-selected-explanations/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d679737e5385227ecd2100b394060797eeb399de2c2821791d96bf30c9488a04","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/test-design.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"The diagnostic lifecycle defines independent invocation identity, start/completion sequence, closed family/severity and nonnegative duration; interrupted/failed clocks remain diagnostic limits.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Allowlisted metadata and bounded safe event replacement exclude raw input, derived request hashes, secrets, environmental identity and prohibited traces/control injection.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Declared filenames under verified private roots use restrictive access and observed containment/identity checks; unsafe existing permissions or substitution degrade without repair.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Finite whole-event JSONL append/rotation and bounded no-steal locking constrain concurrency and traversal to owned files.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Logging state is independent of semantic result/stdout/exit and repository effects; fixed precedence and closed vocabulary checks precede dispatch where required.","number":5,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Console-off suppresses the sole bounded nonrecursive degraded warning; no duplicate semantic console event or generic envelope is added to dedicated recording.","number":6,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-027\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Record bounded private diagnostics without changing command semantics\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Command handling Module shall record only bounded allowlisted private invocation diagnostics on the declared observed path, preserving command semantics, repository state, stdout, and exit behavior when logging is recorded, disabled, degraded, or interrupted.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"A logger can leak raw inputs, damage local state, or become an accidental prerequisite for a successful command.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Available diagnostic events remain useful and private while logging failure or configuration cannot alter the underlying semantic result.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-047 assigns optional diagnostics a non-authoritative role and requires bounded handling of local I/O, privacy, and contention failures.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Operators investigating command behavior\",\n        \"Users whose inputs and local context must remain private\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-010\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"An invocation on the declared observed generic/discovery path reaches minimum logger initialization.\",\n        \"Event writing, clock access, path checks, permissions, locking, or rotation fails or is interrupted.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The private platform user-state logging root or explicitly configured contained root.\",\n        \"Only current contract-owned event and rotation names, outside governed operational records.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Project allowlisted safe event metadata, use closed event/family/severity definitions, and apply bounded whole-event writing, private-path validation, rotation, and lock attempts. Keep diagnostic state and any safe warning independent of semantic execution and result rendering.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Only the current declared observed command path. Primary recording, advanced record-store, and rejected retired commands retain dedicated interfaces and bypass the generic observed wrapper. Existing private-root, restrictive-access, and owned-name rules remain applicable; no daemon, network logging, authoritative audit ledger, or atomic defense against same-user/privileged pathname replacement is added.\",\n      \"limits\": [\n        \"The retained logging contract bounds each encoded event to 16 KiB.\",\n        \"Rotate before an append would exceed 5 MiB and retain the active file plus four archives.\",\n        \"Lock attempts are bounded to ten and 1,000 ms total per event.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"For an observed invocation reaching minimum initialization, attempt the current start and completion events with valid independent invocation identity, timing, closed family/severity, and sequence; completion carries the actual status, exit, and nonnegative duration. Interruption may leave start only, and clock failure degrades diagnostics without changing command meaning.\",\n    \"Events contain only allowlisted metadata. Exclude raw arguments, requests or bodies, request-derived hashes, credentials, arbitrary environment, remotes, usernames/hostnames, absolute repository paths, and the source-prohibited stack traces. Normalize or reject control injection; an oversize event becomes a bounded safe error event rather than a truncation of sensitive input.\",\n    \"Create or rotate only declared owned names within a verified private root using the source restrictive-access rules. Unsafe existing permissions, symlink/non-file/identity/containment failures, observed ancestor substitution, or I/O failure degrade before the unsafe mutation, without permission repair or mutation of governed repository bytes.\",\n    \"Preserve whole supported JSONL events under admitted concurrency and bounded rotation. Exhausted, stale, or unverifiable locks degrade without stealing or removing the lock; no operation escapes the owned root or extends into unbounded traversal.\",\n    \"Recorded, disabled, and degraded logging leave semantic stdout, result, exit, repository mutation, and transaction/recovery behavior unchanged. Apply the current option/environment precedence and reject unknown closed logging values at their declared pre-dispatch boundary without echoing raw input.\",\n    \"Unless console logging is off, a degraded invocation emits only the contract-defined bounded nonrecursive unavailable warning; structured observed projections retain diagnostic state. Do not duplicate an ordinary semantic result as a console event or apply generic envelopes to dedicated recording interfaces.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-010\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-049\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-027\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-047 for the proposed MOD-010 responsibility. Allocates SR-047 criteria 1 through 4 to MOD-010/FUNC-049. AR-028 separately allocates read-only exact invocation lookup, using the same privacy and owned-root boundary. These criteria specify intended observations, not executed product evidence or an adoption of the REM authoring format by the CLI.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-11, CLI-SR-29, CLI-SR-30; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#local-diagnostic-logging\",\n      \"basis\": \"Retains the named current CLI and Record Format obligations at this allocated responsibility boundary. Their detailed formats, supported versions, limits, and observed external-edit boundaries remain authoritative; no runtime behavior or public contract is changed by this draft.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:b33285b2729eb856b3434624680722c22d406737be530e1bc7f8834d631539dc","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-047-keep-local-command-diagnostics-private-and-semantically-independent/AR-027-record-bounded-private-diagnostics-without-changing-command-semantics.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-027","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 6 canonical AR-027 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:7b285e6e49fd80673fbe56702208b9c54614b3303d1927b15b0e09a746b00536","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-049-retain-and-inspect-private-invocation-diagnostics.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a73868f4f79d0e8e41fd3594cb8ef1da0748b4acf6d3922447e70cd9ba44917f","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-047-keep-local-command-diagnostics-private-and-semantically-independent/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"Exact invocation selection scans only the active log and fixed retained rotations within declared byte/file bounds.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Only supported matching events are returned; lookup does not generate its own observed events or expose arbitrary unknown-schema bodies.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Not found is distinct from unavailable and corrupt/unsupported entries; warnings carry safe categories rather than raw log content.","number":3,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Root/permission/identity checks apply on reading too, without permission repair, lock stealing or unbounded filesystem discovery.","number":4,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Log lookup supplies diagnostic observations only; it cannot replay commands, choose recovery or manufacture workflow evidence.","number":5,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-028\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Inspect exact retained invocation diagnostics safely\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Command handling Module shall inspect only the explicitly requested invocation within bounded retained owned log files, return matching supported events and safe availability diagnostics, and leave semantic command execution and governed state unchanged.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"Diagnostic lookup can expose unrelated or unsupported content, silently rerun a command, or misrepresent absent logs as proof that an invocation never occurred.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"An operator sees the available bounded account of the selected invocation and its limitations without new execution, private-data leakage, or implied engineering evidence.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"SR-047 criterion 5 makes exact lookup a read-only diagnostic capability whose usefulness does not confer authority or erase absence uncertainty.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Operators inspecting an exact invocation\",\n        \"Users sharing a private logging environment\",\n        \"Maintainers of MOD-010\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"An actor requests the resolved log directory or events for an exact invocation ID.\",\n        \"Requested events are absent, expired, unavailable, corrupt, or in an unsupported schema.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The current declared owned active/rotated log set inside the verified private logging root.\",\n        \"The public log-inspection result under IF-004, separate from workflow records and recovery.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Validate the exact lookup selector and safe root, scan only bounded retained owned files, select supported matching events, and report safe line-level limitations without exposing raw content or interpreting unknown schemas.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"Read-only directory reporting and exact invocation lookup across the retained active file and four archives defined by the logging contract. No search across unrelated files, command replay, implicit record recovery, repair, archive expansion, or claim that local logs constitute review, workflow, or approval evidence.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Validate the exact invocation identity under the current contract before lookup. Directory reporting returns the resolved logging location without creating governed state; event lookup examines only declared bounded retained owned files through the same private-path and access checks as logging.\",\n    \"Return only matching supported events for the requested invocation. Do not include the lookup invocation's own events, interpret unknown event schemas, or read and return unrelated raw lines.\",\n    \"Distinguish not-found, unavailable, and corrupt-entry outcomes using safe bounded diagnostics. Not-found does not distinguish never-recorded from expired; corrupt or unsupported lines yield bounded warnings without raw content while supported matching events remain available as permitted.\",\n    \"Unsafe paths, unverifiable access, or read failure report the declared unavailability or rejection without following unsafe paths, repairing permissions, altering log history, or exposing invalid raw input.\",\n    \"Lookup does not rerun the original command, perform record recovery, modify authoritative repository state, or manufacture workflow evidence. Its diagnostic failure does not change the original command's semantic result or exit; safe continuation cannot depend on log availability.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [],\n  \"constraints\": [],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-010\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-049\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CLI-ALLOCATION\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-028\",\n      \"basis\": \"Derived from SR-047 for the proposed MOD-010 responsibility. Allocates SR-047 criterion 5 and the lookup contributions to privacy, containment, and semantic independence in criteria 2 through 4. AR-027 owns bounded event production and its shared private-root policy. These criteria specify intended observations, not executed product evidence or an adoption of the REM authoring format by the CLI.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PUBLISHED-CLI\",\n      \"locator\": \"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#CLI-SR-29, CLI-SR-30; design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md#local-diagnostic-logging\",\n      \"basis\": \"Retains the named current CLI and Record Format obligations at this allocated responsibility boundary. Their detailed formats, supported versions, limits, and observed external-edit boundaries remain authoritative; no runtime behavior or public contract is changed by this draft.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:17325c318f4d7578b481dd0d85909a320462f2aa2e8f788ff1c709df0e62c651","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-047-keep-local-command-diagnostics-private-and-semantically-independent/AR-028-inspect-exact-retained-invocation-diagnostics-safely.json"},"limitations":["Design coverage only: no runtime qualification, implemented criterion claim, executed recovery, delivery approval, adoption or authority expansion. Source-observed realization is not proof of target behavior.","Ordinary v2/v4 tasks, qualified maintenance and separately proposed SR-078 history have distinct contracts. Historical v3 executables do not supply successor fallback.","Local associated storage and compatible writer/maintenance assumptions apply. External subjects are observed at declared boundaries, not held globally stable; diagnostics and retrieved records do not confer engineering approval."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-028","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 5 canonical AR-028 criteria, integrated current command/persistence Design with explicit target refinements.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a7ea6434133ae529b7dc4acd02a6375c4f0b98c23307063582f9d9d4c8011e8e","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:7b285e6e49fd80673fbe56702208b9c54614b3303d1927b15b0e09a746b00536","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-049-retain-and-inspect-private-invocation-diagnostics.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a73868f4f79d0e8e41fd3594cb8ef1da0748b4acf6d3922447e70cd9ba44917f","path":"design/requirements/IR-008-operate-on-recorded-engineering-work-through-reliable-explicit-commands/SR-047-keep-local-command-diagnostics-private-and-semantically-independent/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered; implementation and verification remain separately assessed."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-008's canonical requirement methods identify attributable RR, reuse/refinement and justified new needs while preserving stable identities.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"The guidance keeps exclusions and unresolved stakeholder decisions visible and reserves Modules/ARs/tasks for their later accountable owners.","number":2,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-029\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Guide requirement reuse and derivation\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Authoring guidance Module shall guide requirement reuse and derivation within its accountable boundary so that SR-079 can be satisfied without transferring another owner's decisions or state authority.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"The SR-079 obligation crosses guidance, governance or publication boundaries; an unowned contribution can make a locally valid step appear sufficient for the whole workflow.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Explain attributable RR interpretation, existing-owner reuse, refinement and justified creation with preserved identity.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"MOD-008 owns the behavior or state needed for this contribution; separating it preserves one accountable owner while allowing the parent SR to compose several contributors.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Participants relying on Authoring guidance\",\n        \"Authors, reviewers and project decision owners\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When the selected requirement-first workflow exercises SR-079 or reassesses its affected basis.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The MOD-008 responsibility boundary and its declared logical Interfaces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the allocated criteria through the constrained Functions and explicit contract inputs/outcomes; preserve actual actor decisions, subject identity and known limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocated contribution to SR-079; other contributors, independent assessment, physical recording implementation and product activation remain distinct.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Explain attributable RR interpretation, existing-owner reuse, refinement and justified creation with preserved identity.\",\n    \"Expose material exclusions and uncertainty and keep Module/AR/task decisions outside requirement authorship.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The selected project contract, scope and required counterpart contributions are identifiable; absence is reported rather than inferred.\"\n  ],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"This draft allocation neither activates replacement runtime contracts nor proves implementation or satisfaction.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-008\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-032\",\n    \"FUNC-033\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-079; AR-029\",\n      \"basis\": \"Draft integrated design from the accepted requirement-first basis. This defines target responsibility and cooperation, not installed capability, design approval, runtime evidence or SQLite adoption.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:2ec272e3096cdbb386b8df09cf75dd4e5a783232129f82782f4f4f8302f6c520","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-079-reconcile-incoming-requests-with-existing-requirement-owners/AR-029-guide-requirement-reuse-and-derivation.json"},"limitations":["Design assessment only; no runtime implementation, verification, executed adoption, package qualification or external-action authority is claimed.","Current source entrypoints, installed capabilities, project-selected authority and supported recording are distinct. A portable invocation cannot bypass an applicable governed contract; malformed governance is not permission to fall back.","Adoption requires compatible recording for selected work. Established new projects need no historical import; compatible work still needs authority/dependency checks; necessary unavailable migration blocks affected activation while preserving actual authority and history."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-029","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 2 canonical AR-029 criteria; integrated Design contribution with explicit failure, ownership and applicability limits.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:05f2cf53125f83fca4a85ab6c25c6d9cda699e20d20732a7042dc2730cb7accc","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:396489911ab6101e34638b257c875effad9895cb87ef711fe29615d114e5d238","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:dc2586d2d4c135693a8d8211f244133a9430a37c68173b25b7943a59c8782684","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:a08e94ba682a7f58b320393b65b538cea19758b5c069e02a91ed7a4f85753b0b","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/realization/software.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:bb60b1073280d894443e6098e497bc163800f43fbb3c08f8e55d09bb4ee36336","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-008-applicable-engineering-authoring-guidance/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c5f2bacaea51dbddc3bb23988c2cf98b8850770b8e7ba99cee8884191e8e0dc3","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-009-applicable-governed-action-authority/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a40e99dcc2b2ef9df4d63cd83064a726ebc2b76d2e045588cbbd59551e295332","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-010-claim-evidence-applicability-and-coverage/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:41e4298457e86fe690b4027327571f75c8e8cb98e10468f4ae157e3dbac31dd0","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-011-engineering-work-context-and-workflow-adoption/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:965b1f491fd98cb1864153f13d0a52ae73877ec5b8485bccbe4a670e02876e36","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-014-assurance-content-preparation/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7616f27fa93749af2e127663bcfd04fef9579dff8d3ed0c5d00f63f872a245de","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-032-select-canonical-guidance-for-an-authoring-activity.json"},{"identity":"sha256:92153a9115ae4d3b6e0184a95c89e6b3b6ade3f80793c097b715abbe4286c265","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-033-explain-engineering-authoring-and-correction-steps.json"},{"identity":"sha256:37cda3d53b5041ac563370cfb00effc0c5b2fc3d51c3af5273249e9061af9e4c","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9b77090a51b9d33af6a038261e36743682bca6b5cad4b293b99bb1989c2c3e36","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:fc6351e15674dd1cd14b07972e3b89f57756758294b2c2a10cf3483a562180ae","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:966ab13210fd36f3c44388d748827a1e36e1e2a6dc3b58b83f7afe46da077beb","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/workflow.md"},{"identity":"sha256:33306e44a1bd0ae1eae9b7b51c30dcf6bd261619207069e6974a6b3496864572","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d9bef4aadbfd845fc788a4e81a8c9ffb6f33cc7225a6d0acdd72d0e1992ef80f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:62bcaa4c905652e7287c4419c4f7a3422016c6d4f84b2b0a2782b0087c1bce12","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assessment.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9f6b3398a5cbbbc67e9cf98d2daf5d23978ac5174e8275983b0f39bab9af1481","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assurance-content.md"},{"identity":"sha256:43b41da458486e4bedc4801aee579e6de43d62f6527821ad0f7167d01240ce10","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-008-engineering-authoring-guidance/guidance.md"},{"identity":"sha256:bb597226b2064d47ab81b5ccfb4b8f97c1232ac72384a858a928362901432e6b","path":"CONSTITUTION.md"},{"identity":"sha256:02947fd9d6cd22c0a949285f967e70bf0a7dd678650686a7a81aae7eca247852","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-079-reconcile-incoming-requests-with-existing-requirement-owners/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered within the stated contribution; no implementation or verification conclusion."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-012 composes source-bound requirement output through FUNC-053/IF-008, including exact selected definitions and supporting Feature/Scenario scope.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Justified reuse produces a valid proposed basis; unsupported stakeholder decisions return to the requirement owner without synthetic edits.","number":2,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-030\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Compose an attributable proposed requirement basis\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Skill procedures Module shall compose an attributable proposed requirement basis within its accountable boundary so that SR-079 can be satisfied without transferring another owner's decisions or state authority.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"The SR-079 obligation crosses guidance, governance or publication boundaries; an unowned contribution can make a locally valid step appear sufficient for the whole workflow.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Produce the proposed existing/new requirement set and supporting Feature/Scenario analysis with its source and scope.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"MOD-012 owns the behavior or state needed for this contribution; separating it preserves one accountable owner while allowing the parent SR to compose several contributors.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Participants relying on Skill procedures\",\n        \"Authors, reviewers and project decision owners\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When the selected requirement-first workflow exercises SR-079 or reassesses its affected basis.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The MOD-012 responsibility boundary and its declared logical Interfaces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the allocated criteria through the constrained Functions and explicit contract inputs/outcomes; preserve actual actor decisions, subject identity and known limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocated contribution to SR-079; other contributors, independent assessment, physical recording implementation and product activation remain distinct.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Produce the proposed existing/new requirement set and supporting Feature/Scenario analysis with its source and scope.\",\n    \"Accept justified reuse without synthetic edits; return unresolved stakeholder decisions to their owner.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The selected project contract, scope and required counterpart contributions are identifiable; absence is reported rather than inferred.\"\n  ],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"This draft allocation neither activates replacement runtime contracts nor proves implementation or satisfaction.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-012\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-051\",\n    \"FUNC-053\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-079; AR-030\",\n      \"basis\": \"Draft integrated design from the accepted requirement-first basis. This defines target responsibility and cooperation, not installed capability, design approval, runtime evidence or SQLite adoption.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:ed56084ef2a88a485269589a825b609b4f74d5f357da4fd07263d22d884c7d86","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-079-reconcile-incoming-requests-with-existing-requirement-owners/AR-030-compose-an-attributable-proposed-requirement-basis.json"},"limitations":["Design assessment only; no runtime implementation, verification, executed adoption, package qualification or external-action authority is claimed.","Current source entrypoints, installed capabilities, project-selected authority and supported recording are distinct. A portable invocation cannot bypass an applicable governed contract; malformed governance is not permission to fall back.","Adoption requires compatible recording for selected work. Established new projects need no historical import; compatible work still needs authority/dependency checks; necessary unavailable migration blocks affected activation while preserving actual authority and history."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-030","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 2 canonical AR-030 criteria; integrated Design contribution with explicit failure, ownership and applicability limits.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:05f2cf53125f83fca4a85ab6c25c6d9cda699e20d20732a7042dc2730cb7accc","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:396489911ab6101e34638b257c875effad9895cb87ef711fe29615d114e5d238","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:dc2586d2d4c135693a8d8211f244133a9430a37c68173b25b7943a59c8782684","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:a08e94ba682a7f58b320393b65b538cea19758b5c069e02a91ed7a4f85753b0b","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/realization/software.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:bb60b1073280d894443e6098e497bc163800f43fbb3c08f8e55d09bb4ee36336","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-008-applicable-engineering-authoring-guidance/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c5f2bacaea51dbddc3bb23988c2cf98b8850770b8e7ba99cee8884191e8e0dc3","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-009-applicable-governed-action-authority/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a40e99dcc2b2ef9df4d63cd83064a726ebc2b76d2e045588cbbd59551e295332","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-010-claim-evidence-applicability-and-coverage/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:41e4298457e86fe690b4027327571f75c8e8cb98e10468f4ae157e3dbac31dd0","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-011-engineering-work-context-and-workflow-adoption/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:965b1f491fd98cb1864153f13d0a52ae73877ec5b8485bccbe4a670e02876e36","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-014-assurance-content-preparation/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c8152391e8dc91c31d65e24620ef5380cf62f0c1088be69833e9db0b0923ab16","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-051-prepare-a-portable-or-governed-capability-invocation.json"},{"identity":"sha256:aa83665c5155a32aa129ebb62e1179f03935efc4cb3b6a06613fe709deb02211","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-053-guide-a-bounded-specialist-engineering-activity.json"},{"identity":"sha256:37cda3d53b5041ac563370cfb00effc0c5b2fc3d51c3af5273249e9061af9e4c","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9b77090a51b9d33af6a038261e36743682bca6b5cad4b293b99bb1989c2c3e36","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:fc6351e15674dd1cd14b07972e3b89f57756758294b2c2a10cf3483a562180ae","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:966ab13210fd36f3c44388d748827a1e36e1e2a6dc3b58b83f7afe46da077beb","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/workflow.md"},{"identity":"sha256:33306e44a1bd0ae1eae9b7b51c30dcf6bd261619207069e6974a6b3496864572","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d9bef4aadbfd845fc788a4e81a8c9ffb6f33cc7225a6d0acdd72d0e1992ef80f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:62bcaa4c905652e7287c4419c4f7a3422016c6d4f84b2b0a2782b0087c1bce12","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assessment.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9f6b3398a5cbbbc67e9cf98d2daf5d23978ac5174e8275983b0f39bab9af1481","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assurance-content.md"},{"identity":"sha256:43b41da458486e4bedc4801aee579e6de43d62f6527821ad0f7167d01240ce10","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-008-engineering-authoring-guidance/guidance.md"},{"identity":"sha256:bb597226b2064d47ab81b5ccfb4b8f97c1232ac72384a858a928362901432e6b","path":"CONSTITUTION.md"},{"identity":"sha256:02947fd9d6cd22c0a949285f967e70bf0a7dd678650686a7a81aae7eca247852","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-079-reconcile-incoming-requests-with-existing-requirement-owners/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered within the stated contribution; no implementation or verification conclusion."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-007 assurance preparation preserves the supplied requirement judgment's exact subjects, basis, actor, contrary evidence and limitations before explicit retention.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Requirement validity is assessed independently of unfinished Function/AR allocation, and old proposal approval cannot stand in for the first requirement gate.","number":2,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-031\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Preserve exact requirement review scope and basis\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Review and verification Module shall preserve exact requirement review scope and basis within its accountable boundary so that SR-080 can be satisfied without transferring another owner's decisions or state authority.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"The SR-080 obligation crosses guidance, governance or publication boundaries; an unowned contribution can make a locally valid step appear sufficient for the whole workflow.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Bind the supplied requirement judgment to exact obligations and supporting analysis, actor provenance, contrary evidence and limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"MOD-007 owns the behavior or state needed for this contribution; separating it preserves one accountable owner while allowing the parent SR to compose several contributors.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Participants relying on Review and verification\",\n        \"Authors, reviewers and project decision owners\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When the selected requirement-first workflow exercises SR-080 or reassesses its affected basis.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The MOD-007 responsibility boundary and its declared logical Interfaces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the allocated criteria through the constrained Functions and explicit contract inputs/outcomes; preserve actual actor decisions, subject identity and known limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocated contribution to SR-080; other contributors, independent assessment, physical recording implementation and product activation remain distinct.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Bind the supplied requirement judgment to exact obligations and supporting analysis, actor provenance, contrary evidence and limitations.\",\n    \"Do not demand downstream Function or AR coverage to assess requirement validity; old proposal approval is not substitute support.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The selected project contract, scope and required counterpart contributions are identifiable; absence is reported rather than inferred.\"\n  ],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"This draft allocation neither activates replacement runtime contracts nor proves implementation or satisfaction.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-007\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-029\",\n    \"FUNC-030\",\n    \"FUNC-031\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-080; AR-031\",\n      \"basis\": \"Draft integrated design from the accepted requirement-first basis. This defines target responsibility and cooperation, not installed capability, design approval, runtime evidence or SQLite adoption.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:03bd539cf1bcf3402fb03830a5fb7d809a57d9aa8af7ee7b8e535d64e6657415","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-080-establish-the-reviewed-requirement-basis-before-dependent-design/AR-031-preserve-exact-requirement-review-scope-and-basis.json"},"limitations":["Design assessment only; no runtime implementation, verification, executed adoption, package qualification or external-action authority is claimed.","Current source entrypoints, installed capabilities, project-selected authority and supported recording are distinct. A portable invocation cannot bypass an applicable governed contract; malformed governance is not permission to fall back.","Adoption requires compatible recording for selected work. Established new projects need no historical import; compatible work still needs authority/dependency checks; necessary unavailable migration blocks affected activation while preserving actual authority and history."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-031","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 2 canonical AR-031 criteria; integrated Design contribution with explicit failure, ownership and applicability limits.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:05f2cf53125f83fca4a85ab6c25c6d9cda699e20d20732a7042dc2730cb7accc","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:396489911ab6101e34638b257c875effad9895cb87ef711fe29615d114e5d238","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:dc2586d2d4c135693a8d8211f244133a9430a37c68173b25b7943a59c8782684","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:a08e94ba682a7f58b320393b65b538cea19758b5c069e02a91ed7a4f85753b0b","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/realization/software.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:bb60b1073280d894443e6098e497bc163800f43fbb3c08f8e55d09bb4ee36336","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-008-applicable-engineering-authoring-guidance/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c5f2bacaea51dbddc3bb23988c2cf98b8850770b8e7ba99cee8884191e8e0dc3","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-009-applicable-governed-action-authority/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a40e99dcc2b2ef9df4d63cd83064a726ebc2b76d2e045588cbbd59551e295332","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-010-claim-evidence-applicability-and-coverage/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:41e4298457e86fe690b4027327571f75c8e8cb98e10468f4ae157e3dbac31dd0","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-011-engineering-work-context-and-workflow-adoption/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:965b1f491fd98cb1864153f13d0a52ae73877ec5b8485bccbe4a670e02876e36","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-014-assurance-content-preparation/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a52db28adb589ab258420815dfaccfc743876128145cd62404c5df7968eee51b","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-029-assess-evidence-applicability-to-a-declared-claim.json"},{"identity":"sha256:85db55d933a26a2b6840d630caab1172dc9c820486bfca845444ab3fdf81fc59","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-030-expose-claim-criterion-coverage-and-contradictory-evidence.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cdfb0de0bee02ac23889aec83011b1f10878f8f15f03afef1e50648b8b184381","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-031-record-scoped-engineering-judgments-and-their-basis.json"},{"identity":"sha256:37cda3d53b5041ac563370cfb00effc0c5b2fc3d51c3af5273249e9061af9e4c","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9b77090a51b9d33af6a038261e36743682bca6b5cad4b293b99bb1989c2c3e36","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:fc6351e15674dd1cd14b07972e3b89f57756758294b2c2a10cf3483a562180ae","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:966ab13210fd36f3c44388d748827a1e36e1e2a6dc3b58b83f7afe46da077beb","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/workflow.md"},{"identity":"sha256:33306e44a1bd0ae1eae9b7b51c30dcf6bd261619207069e6974a6b3496864572","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d9bef4aadbfd845fc788a4e81a8c9ffb6f33cc7225a6d0acdd72d0e1992ef80f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:62bcaa4c905652e7287c4419c4f7a3422016c6d4f84b2b0a2782b0087c1bce12","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assessment.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9f6b3398a5cbbbc67e9cf98d2daf5d23978ac5174e8275983b0f39bab9af1481","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assurance-content.md"},{"identity":"sha256:43b41da458486e4bedc4801aee579e6de43d62f6527821ad0f7167d01240ce10","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-008-engineering-authoring-guidance/guidance.md"},{"identity":"sha256:bb597226b2064d47ab81b5ccfb4b8f97c1232ac72384a858a928362901432e6b","path":"CONSTITUTION.md"},{"identity":"sha256:e49b224c096fe465471e511294eacff82bbeaa5e92d9d34948e15b02e025d1c5","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-080-establish-the-reviewed-requirement-basis-before-dependent-design/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered within the stated contribution; no implementation or verification conclusion."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-012 requests independent review of both changed and reused requirement bases before dependent Design reliance.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Accepted requirements enable only authorized next work; unfinished Design remains explicit and material requirement changes require renewed applicability assessment.","number":2,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-032\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Route design from an applicable requirement basis\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Skill procedures Module shall route design from an applicable requirement basis within its accountable boundary so that SR-080 can be satisfied without transferring another owner's decisions or state authority.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"The SR-080 obligation crosses guidance, governance or publication boundaries; an unowned contribution can make a locally valid step appear sufficient for the whole workflow.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Request the first requirement gate, including review of reuse conclusions, before dependent design relies on the basis.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"MOD-012 owns the behavior or state needed for this contribution; separating it preserves one accountable owner while allowing the parent SR to compose several contributors.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Participants relying on Skill procedures\",\n        \"Authors, reviewers and project decision owners\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When the selected requirement-first workflow exercises SR-080 or reassesses its affected basis.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The MOD-012 responsibility boundary and its declared logical Interfaces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the allocated criteria through the constrained Functions and explicit contract inputs/outcomes; preserve actual actor decisions, subject identity and known limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocated contribution to SR-080; other contributors, independent assessment, physical recording implementation and product activation remain distinct.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Request the first requirement gate, including review of reuse conclusions, before dependent design relies on the basis.\",\n    \"Permit accepted requirements with unfinished design to proceed only to the authorized next work; changed requirements require applicability reassessment.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The selected project contract, scope and required counterpart contributions are identifiable; absence is reported rather than inferred.\"\n  ],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"This draft allocation neither activates replacement runtime contracts nor proves implementation or satisfaction.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-012\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-053\",\n    \"FUNC-054\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-080; AR-032\",\n      \"basis\": \"Draft integrated design from the accepted requirement-first basis. This defines target responsibility and cooperation, not installed capability, design approval, runtime evidence or SQLite adoption.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:76f3532f75698e7349cc880b00c817787addef8f6ad53f89ffcb05fa5686d585","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-080-establish-the-reviewed-requirement-basis-before-dependent-design/AR-032-route-design-from-an-applicable-requirement-basis.json"},"limitations":["Design assessment only; no runtime implementation, verification, executed adoption, package qualification or external-action authority is claimed.","Current source entrypoints, installed capabilities, project-selected authority and supported recording are distinct. A portable invocation cannot bypass an applicable governed contract; malformed governance is not permission to fall back.","Adoption requires compatible recording for selected work. Established new projects need no historical import; compatible work still needs authority/dependency checks; necessary unavailable migration blocks affected activation while preserving actual authority and history."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-032","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 2 canonical AR-032 criteria; integrated Design contribution with explicit failure, ownership and applicability limits.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:05f2cf53125f83fca4a85ab6c25c6d9cda699e20d20732a7042dc2730cb7accc","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:396489911ab6101e34638b257c875effad9895cb87ef711fe29615d114e5d238","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:dc2586d2d4c135693a8d8211f244133a9430a37c68173b25b7943a59c8782684","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:a08e94ba682a7f58b320393b65b538cea19758b5c069e02a91ed7a4f85753b0b","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/realization/software.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:bb60b1073280d894443e6098e497bc163800f43fbb3c08f8e55d09bb4ee36336","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-008-applicable-engineering-authoring-guidance/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c5f2bacaea51dbddc3bb23988c2cf98b8850770b8e7ba99cee8884191e8e0dc3","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-009-applicable-governed-action-authority/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a40e99dcc2b2ef9df4d63cd83064a726ebc2b76d2e045588cbbd59551e295332","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-010-claim-evidence-applicability-and-coverage/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:41e4298457e86fe690b4027327571f75c8e8cb98e10468f4ae157e3dbac31dd0","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-011-engineering-work-context-and-workflow-adoption/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:965b1f491fd98cb1864153f13d0a52ae73877ec5b8485bccbe4a670e02876e36","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-014-assurance-content-preparation/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:aa83665c5155a32aa129ebb62e1179f03935efc4cb3b6a06613fe709deb02211","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-053-guide-a-bounded-specialist-engineering-activity.json"},{"identity":"sha256:72ed79db6e5aabe502b0d82ce6215409a69dfb1610502dcd458250607f97ba1a","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-054-determine-an-applicable-engineering-handoff.json"},{"identity":"sha256:37cda3d53b5041ac563370cfb00effc0c5b2fc3d51c3af5273249e9061af9e4c","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9b77090a51b9d33af6a038261e36743682bca6b5cad4b293b99bb1989c2c3e36","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:fc6351e15674dd1cd14b07972e3b89f57756758294b2c2a10cf3483a562180ae","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:966ab13210fd36f3c44388d748827a1e36e1e2a6dc3b58b83f7afe46da077beb","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/workflow.md"},{"identity":"sha256:33306e44a1bd0ae1eae9b7b51c30dcf6bd261619207069e6974a6b3496864572","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d9bef4aadbfd845fc788a4e81a8c9ffb6f33cc7225a6d0acdd72d0e1992ef80f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:62bcaa4c905652e7287c4419c4f7a3422016c6d4f84b2b0a2782b0087c1bce12","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assessment.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9f6b3398a5cbbbc67e9cf98d2daf5d23978ac5174e8275983b0f39bab9af1481","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assurance-content.md"},{"identity":"sha256:43b41da458486e4bedc4801aee579e6de43d62f6527821ad0f7167d01240ce10","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-008-engineering-authoring-guidance/guidance.md"},{"identity":"sha256:bb597226b2064d47ab81b5ccfb4b8f97c1232ac72384a858a928362901432e6b","path":"CONSTITUTION.md"},{"identity":"sha256:e49b224c096fe465471e511294eacff82bbeaa5e92d9d34948e15b02e025d1c5","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-080-establish-the-reviewed-requirement-basis-before-dependent-design/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered within the stated contribution; no implementation or verification conclusion."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-008 methods separate stakeholder obligations, logical behavior and architectural responsibility/realization without moving their authorship to a common wrapper.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Architecture Allocation and appropriate views guide analysis, not extra approvals; plans cannot replace required allocated obligations.","number":2,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-033\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Explain distinct requirement and design authorship\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Authoring guidance Module shall explain distinct requirement and design authorship within its accountable boundary so that SR-081 can be satisfied without transferring another owner's decisions or state authority.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"The SR-081 obligation crosses guidance, governance or publication boundaries; an unowned contribution can make a locally valid step appear sufficient for the whole workflow.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Keep IR/SR and stakeholder intent, logical Functions, and Module/Interface/AR realization under their respective authoring methods.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"MOD-008 owns the behavior or state needed for this contribution; separating it preserves one accountable owner while allowing the parent SR to compose several contributors.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Participants relying on Authoring guidance\",\n        \"Authors, reviewers and project decision owners\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When the selected requirement-first workflow exercises SR-081 or reassesses its affected basis.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The MOD-008 responsibility boundary and its declared logical Interfaces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the allocated criteria through the constrained Functions and explicit contract inputs/outcomes; preserve actual actor decisions, subject identity and known limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocated contribution to SR-081; other contributors, independent assessment, physical recording implementation and product activation remain distinct.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Keep IR/SR and stakeholder intent, logical Functions, and Module/Interface/AR realization under their respective authoring methods.\",\n    \"Explain allocation and applicable 4+1 methods without introducing separate technique approvals or substituting delivery tasks for ARs.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The selected project contract, scope and required counterpart contributions are identifiable; absence is reported rather than inferred.\"\n  ],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"This draft allocation neither activates replacement runtime contracts nor proves implementation or satisfaction.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-008\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-032\",\n    \"FUNC-033\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-081; AR-033\",\n      \"basis\": \"Draft integrated design from the accepted requirement-first basis. This defines target responsibility and cooperation, not installed capability, design approval, runtime evidence or SQLite adoption.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:c45222e41220bc77adefa93d87caac6d01d9930d24e9950ac36c03ebdd827f3c","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-081-preserve-distinct-authoring-ownership-and-integrated-design-assessment/AR-033-explain-distinct-requirement-and-design-authorship.json"},"limitations":["Design assessment only; no runtime implementation, verification, executed adoption, package qualification or external-action authority is claimed.","Current source entrypoints, installed capabilities, project-selected authority and supported recording are distinct. A portable invocation cannot bypass an applicable governed contract; malformed governance is not permission to fall back.","Adoption requires compatible recording for selected work. Established new projects need no historical import; compatible work still needs authority/dependency checks; necessary unavailable migration blocks affected activation while preserving actual authority and history."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-033","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 2 canonical AR-033 criteria; integrated Design contribution with explicit failure, ownership and applicability limits.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:05f2cf53125f83fca4a85ab6c25c6d9cda699e20d20732a7042dc2730cb7accc","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:396489911ab6101e34638b257c875effad9895cb87ef711fe29615d114e5d238","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:dc2586d2d4c135693a8d8211f244133a9430a37c68173b25b7943a59c8782684","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:a08e94ba682a7f58b320393b65b538cea19758b5c069e02a91ed7a4f85753b0b","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/realization/software.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:bb60b1073280d894443e6098e497bc163800f43fbb3c08f8e55d09bb4ee36336","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-008-applicable-engineering-authoring-guidance/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c5f2bacaea51dbddc3bb23988c2cf98b8850770b8e7ba99cee8884191e8e0dc3","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-009-applicable-governed-action-authority/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a40e99dcc2b2ef9df4d63cd83064a726ebc2b76d2e045588cbbd59551e295332","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-010-claim-evidence-applicability-and-coverage/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:41e4298457e86fe690b4027327571f75c8e8cb98e10468f4ae157e3dbac31dd0","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-011-engineering-work-context-and-workflow-adoption/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:965b1f491fd98cb1864153f13d0a52ae73877ec5b8485bccbe4a670e02876e36","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-014-assurance-content-preparation/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:7616f27fa93749af2e127663bcfd04fef9579dff8d3ed0c5d00f63f872a245de","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-032-select-canonical-guidance-for-an-authoring-activity.json"},{"identity":"sha256:92153a9115ae4d3b6e0184a95c89e6b3b6ade3f80793c097b715abbe4286c265","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-033-explain-engineering-authoring-and-correction-steps.json"},{"identity":"sha256:37cda3d53b5041ac563370cfb00effc0c5b2fc3d51c3af5273249e9061af9e4c","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9b77090a51b9d33af6a038261e36743682bca6b5cad4b293b99bb1989c2c3e36","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:fc6351e15674dd1cd14b07972e3b89f57756758294b2c2a10cf3483a562180ae","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:966ab13210fd36f3c44388d748827a1e36e1e2a6dc3b58b83f7afe46da077beb","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/workflow.md"},{"identity":"sha256:33306e44a1bd0ae1eae9b7b51c30dcf6bd261619207069e6974a6b3496864572","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d9bef4aadbfd845fc788a4e81a8c9ffb6f33cc7225a6d0acdd72d0e1992ef80f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:62bcaa4c905652e7287c4419c4f7a3422016c6d4f84b2b0a2782b0087c1bce12","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assessment.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9f6b3398a5cbbbc67e9cf98d2daf5d23978ac5174e8275983b0f39bab9af1481","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assurance-content.md"},{"identity":"sha256:43b41da458486e4bedc4801aee579e6de43d62f6527821ad0f7167d01240ce10","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-008-engineering-authoring-guidance/guidance.md"},{"identity":"sha256:bb597226b2064d47ab81b5ccfb4b8f97c1232ac72384a858a928362901432e6b","path":"CONSTITUTION.md"},{"identity":"sha256:7826faf5e602cafb5fa149f0ad5b6fa855635c0f594165fc8f976aa88a615f49","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-081-preserve-distinct-authoring-ownership-and-integrated-design-assessment/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered within the stated contribution; no implementation or verification conclusion."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-012 prepares the complete affected logical and architectural composition with its accepted requirements for one integrated review before planning.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"The correction matrix preserves iteration and exact assessed scope while routing needs, behavior and boundary/allocation defects to their respective authors.","number":2,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-034\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Compose integrated design assessment and correction handoffs\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Skill procedures Module shall compose integrated design assessment and correction handoffs within its accountable boundary so that SR-081 can be satisfied without transferring another owner's decisions or state authority.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"The SR-081 obligation crosses guidance, governance or publication boundaries; an unowned contribution can make a locally valid step appear sufficient for the whole workflow.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Present the complete affected System and Architecture Design against the accepted requirements to one integrated review before planning.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"MOD-012 owns the behavior or state needed for this contribution; separating it preserves one accountable owner while allowing the parent SR to compose several contributors.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Participants relying on Skill procedures\",\n        \"Authors, reviewers and project decision owners\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When the selected requirement-first workflow exercises SR-081 or reassesses its affected basis.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The MOD-012 responsibility boundary and its declared logical Interfaces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the allocated criteria through the constrained Functions and explicit contract inputs/outcomes; preserve actual actor decisions, subject identity and known limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocated contribution to SR-081; other contributors, independent assessment, physical recording implementation and product activation remain distinct.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Present the complete affected System and Architecture Design against the accepted requirements to one integrated review before planning.\",\n    \"Route changed needs to Requirement Analysis, behavior to System Design, and boundary/allocation defects to Architecture Design; preserve iteration and assessed scope.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The selected project contract, scope and required counterpart contributions are identifiable; absence is reported rather than inferred.\"\n  ],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"This draft allocation neither activates replacement runtime contracts nor proves implementation or satisfaction.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-012\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-053\",\n    \"FUNC-054\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-081; AR-034\",\n      \"basis\": \"Draft integrated design from the accepted requirement-first basis. This defines target responsibility and cooperation, not installed capability, design approval, runtime evidence or SQLite adoption.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:1e1b12b75f240ded3e1520a94aefcba4c215049429f42ddbc83eb9b12b140537","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-081-preserve-distinct-authoring-ownership-and-integrated-design-assessment/AR-034-compose-integrated-design-assessment-and-correction-handoffs.json"},"limitations":["Design assessment only; no runtime implementation, verification, executed adoption, package qualification or external-action authority is claimed.","Current source entrypoints, installed capabilities, project-selected authority and supported recording are distinct. A portable invocation cannot bypass an applicable governed contract; malformed governance is not permission to fall back.","Adoption requires compatible recording for selected work. Established new projects need no historical import; compatible work still needs authority/dependency checks; necessary unavailable migration blocks affected activation while preserving actual authority and history."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-034","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 2 canonical AR-034 criteria; integrated Design contribution with explicit failure, ownership and applicability limits.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:05f2cf53125f83fca4a85ab6c25c6d9cda699e20d20732a7042dc2730cb7accc","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:396489911ab6101e34638b257c875effad9895cb87ef711fe29615d114e5d238","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:dc2586d2d4c135693a8d8211f244133a9430a37c68173b25b7943a59c8782684","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:a08e94ba682a7f58b320393b65b538cea19758b5c069e02a91ed7a4f85753b0b","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/realization/software.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:bb60b1073280d894443e6098e497bc163800f43fbb3c08f8e55d09bb4ee36336","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-008-applicable-engineering-authoring-guidance/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c5f2bacaea51dbddc3bb23988c2cf98b8850770b8e7ba99cee8884191e8e0dc3","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-009-applicable-governed-action-authority/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a40e99dcc2b2ef9df4d63cd83064a726ebc2b76d2e045588cbbd59551e295332","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-010-claim-evidence-applicability-and-coverage/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:41e4298457e86fe690b4027327571f75c8e8cb98e10468f4ae157e3dbac31dd0","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-011-engineering-work-context-and-workflow-adoption/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:965b1f491fd98cb1864153f13d0a52ae73877ec5b8485bccbe4a670e02876e36","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-014-assurance-content-preparation/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:aa83665c5155a32aa129ebb62e1179f03935efc4cb3b6a06613fe709deb02211","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-053-guide-a-bounded-specialist-engineering-activity.json"},{"identity":"sha256:72ed79db6e5aabe502b0d82ce6215409a69dfb1610502dcd458250607f97ba1a","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-054-determine-an-applicable-engineering-handoff.json"},{"identity":"sha256:37cda3d53b5041ac563370cfb00effc0c5b2fc3d51c3af5273249e9061af9e4c","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9b77090a51b9d33af6a038261e36743682bca6b5cad4b293b99bb1989c2c3e36","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:fc6351e15674dd1cd14b07972e3b89f57756758294b2c2a10cf3483a562180ae","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:966ab13210fd36f3c44388d748827a1e36e1e2a6dc3b58b83f7afe46da077beb","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/workflow.md"},{"identity":"sha256:33306e44a1bd0ae1eae9b7b51c30dcf6bd261619207069e6974a6b3496864572","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d9bef4aadbfd845fc788a4e81a8c9ffb6f33cc7225a6d0acdd72d0e1992ef80f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:62bcaa4c905652e7287c4419c4f7a3422016c6d4f84b2b0a2782b0087c1bce12","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assessment.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9f6b3398a5cbbbc67e9cf98d2daf5d23978ac5174e8275983b0f39bab9af1481","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assurance-content.md"},{"identity":"sha256:43b41da458486e4bedc4801aee579e6de43d62f6527821ad0f7167d01240ce10","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-008-engineering-authoring-guidance/guidance.md"},{"identity":"sha256:bb597226b2064d47ab81b5ccfb4b8f97c1232ac72384a858a928362901432e6b","path":"CONSTITUTION.md"},{"identity":"sha256:7826faf5e602cafb5fa149f0ad5b6fa855635c0f594165fc8f976aa88a615f49","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-081-preserve-distinct-authoring-ownership-and-integrated-design-assessment/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered within the stated contribution; no implementation or verification conclusion."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-006's current handoff retains milestone scope, real checks, defect dispositions and dependencies without requiring a reviewer or milestone approval field.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Authority interpretation and unresolved work yield exact blockers; progress and next-step suggestions cannot grant permission or settle a gate.","number":2,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-035\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Retain checked work progress independently of review approval\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Change control Module shall retain checked work progress independently of review approval within its accountable boundary so that SR-082 can be satisfied without transferring another owner's decisions or state authority.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"The SR-082 obligation crosses guidance, governance or publication boundaries; an unowned contribution can make a locally valid step appear sufficient for the whole workflow.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Keep authorized milestone scope, required check results, known-defect dispositions and dependencies retrievable without a mandatory milestone review ID.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"MOD-006 owns the behavior or state needed for this contribution; separating it preserves one accountable owner while allowing the parent SR to compose several contributors.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Participants relying on Change control\",\n        \"Authors, reviewers and project decision owners\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When the selected requirement-first workflow exercises SR-082 or reassesses its affected basis.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The MOD-006 responsibility boundary and its declared logical Interfaces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the allocated criteria through the constrained Functions and explicit contract inputs/outcomes; preserve actual actor decisions, subject identity and known limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocated contribution to SR-082; other contributors, independent assessment, physical recording implementation and product activation remain distinct.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Keep authorized milestone scope, required check results, known-defect dispositions and dependencies retrievable without a mandatory milestone review ID.\",\n    \"Return uncovered authority or unresolved work as a blocker; progress and suggested next work do not grant permission or settle a gate.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The selected project contract, scope and required counterpart contributions are identifiable; absence is reported rather than inferred.\"\n  ],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"This draft allocation neither activates replacement runtime contracts nor proves implementation or satisfaction.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-006\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-025\",\n    \"FUNC-026\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-082; AR-035\",\n      \"basis\": \"Draft integrated design from the accepted requirement-first basis. This defines target responsibility and cooperation, not installed capability, design approval, runtime evidence or SQLite adoption.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:b3081a2f1fcdae4cf085da5588c8573e5e10a9936827c22d11455d2fb593f62c","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-082-require-one-whole-change-review-gate-after-checked-implementation/AR-035-retain-checked-work-progress-independently-of-review-approval.json"},"limitations":["Design assessment only; no runtime implementation, verification, executed adoption, package qualification or external-action authority is claimed.","Current source entrypoints, installed capabilities, project-selected authority and supported recording are distinct. A portable invocation cannot bypass an applicable governed contract; malformed governance is not permission to fall back.","Adoption requires compatible recording for selected work. Established new projects need no historical import; compatible work still needs authority/dependency checks; necessary unavailable migration blocks affected activation while preserving actual authority and history."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-035","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 2 canonical AR-035 criteria; integrated Design contribution with explicit failure, ownership and applicability limits.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:05f2cf53125f83fca4a85ab6c25c6d9cda699e20d20732a7042dc2730cb7accc","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:396489911ab6101e34638b257c875effad9895cb87ef711fe29615d114e5d238","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:dc2586d2d4c135693a8d8211f244133a9430a37c68173b25b7943a59c8782684","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:a08e94ba682a7f58b320393b65b538cea19758b5c069e02a91ed7a4f85753b0b","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/realization/software.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:bb60b1073280d894443e6098e497bc163800f43fbb3c08f8e55d09bb4ee36336","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-008-applicable-engineering-authoring-guidance/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c5f2bacaea51dbddc3bb23988c2cf98b8850770b8e7ba99cee8884191e8e0dc3","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-009-applicable-governed-action-authority/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a40e99dcc2b2ef9df4d63cd83064a726ebc2b76d2e045588cbbd59551e295332","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-010-claim-evidence-applicability-and-coverage/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:41e4298457e86fe690b4027327571f75c8e8cb98e10468f4ae157e3dbac31dd0","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-011-engineering-work-context-and-workflow-adoption/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:965b1f491fd98cb1864153f13d0a52ae73877ec5b8485bccbe4a670e02876e36","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-014-assurance-content-preparation/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:b5bbfbf03874ea29120c3443bd5efc8160f8cbbf230286fde5316d5fee495ef1","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-025-retain-and-retrieve-activity-specific-change-context.json"},{"identity":"sha256:e2d0fbfe210afa2888bbdd1061ab5a4b3783292b44a7ab374b73beaa3203d869","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-026-determine-applicable-authority-before-governed-actions.json"},{"identity":"sha256:37cda3d53b5041ac563370cfb00effc0c5b2fc3d51c3af5273249e9061af9e4c","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9b77090a51b9d33af6a038261e36743682bca6b5cad4b293b99bb1989c2c3e36","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:fc6351e15674dd1cd14b07972e3b89f57756758294b2c2a10cf3483a562180ae","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:966ab13210fd36f3c44388d748827a1e36e1e2a6dc3b58b83f7afe46da077beb","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/workflow.md"},{"identity":"sha256:33306e44a1bd0ae1eae9b7b51c30dcf6bd261619207069e6974a6b3496864572","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d9bef4aadbfd845fc788a4e81a8c9ffb6f33cc7225a6d0acdd72d0e1992ef80f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:62bcaa4c905652e7287c4419c4f7a3422016c6d4f84b2b0a2782b0087c1bce12","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assessment.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9f6b3398a5cbbbc67e9cf98d2daf5d23978ac5174e8275983b0f39bab9af1481","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assurance-content.md"},{"identity":"sha256:43b41da458486e4bedc4801aee579e6de43d62f6527821ad0f7167d01240ce10","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-008-engineering-authoring-guidance/guidance.md"},{"identity":"sha256:bb597226b2064d47ab81b5ccfb4b8f97c1232ac72384a858a928362901432e6b","path":"CONSTITUTION.md"},{"identity":"sha256:b1f763a877947390ed6a24448c159dd370da5b341fbeca38e090291360c20a08","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-082-require-one-whole-change-review-gate-after-checked-implementation/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered within the stated contribution; no implementation or verification conclusion."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-007 distinguishes advisory from formal judgment and retains enough exact assessed support for current reliance and proportionate reassessment.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"The parent impact table requires cumulative actual-effect reasoning for harmless continuation, independent material correction review and explicit uncertainty, preserving whole-change adequacy and original meaning.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Verify remains a separate judgment: engineering defects return for owned correction and affected review, while unchanged-subject evidence retries alone do not restart the gate.","number":3,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-036\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Maintain whole change review standing and applicability\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Review and verification Module shall maintain attributable current review standing, unresolved findings and applicable support within one whole-change gate, without requiring permanent storage of superseded assessment attempts.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"The SR-082 obligation crosses guidance, governance or publication boundaries; an unowned contribution can make a locally valid step appear sufficient for the whole workflow.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Keep advisory feedback distinct from formal approval, retain enough assessed basis for current reliance, and support proportionate reassessment.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"MOD-007 owns the behavior or state needed for this contribution; separating it preserves one accountable owner while allowing the parent SR to compose several contributors.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Participants relying on Review and verification\",\n        \"Authors, reviewers and project decision owners\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When the selected requirement-first workflow exercises SR-082 or reassesses its affected basis.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The MOD-007 responsibility boundary and its declared logical Interfaces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the allocated criteria through the constrained Functions and explicit contract inputs/outcomes; preserve actual actor decisions, subject identity and known limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocated contribution to SR-082; other contributors, independent assessment, physical recording implementation and product activation remain distinct.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Keep advisory feedback distinct from formal approval, retain enough assessed basis for current reliance, and support proportionate reassessment.\",\n    \"Assess changes and affected interactions proportionately. Permit explicit justified applicability continuation after harmless edits without a new Review; material corrections require independent reassessment and unknown impact remains unresolved. Retain whole-change adequacy, cumulative change visibility and original judgment meanings.\",\n    \"Keep Verify distinct; engineering defects require owned correction and affected review, while unchanged-subject evidence retries do not automatically restart review.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The selected project contract, scope and required counterpart contributions are identifiable; absence is reported rather than inferred.\"\n  ],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"This draft allocation neither activates replacement runtime contracts nor proves implementation or satisfaction.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-007\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-029\",\n    \"FUNC-030\",\n    \"FUNC-031\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-082; AR-036\",\n      \"basis\": \"Draft integrated design from the accepted requirement-first basis. This defines target responsibility and cooperation, not installed capability, design approval, runtime evidence or SQLite adoption.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-PROPORTIONATE-REVIEW\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-036\",\n      \"basis\": \"User-directed refinement of review applicability after subsequent edits: preserve original judgments, allow justified harmless-change continuation and independently reassess material effects. Author-assessed design/requirement refinement only; no runtime adoption or independent approval is claimed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-CURRENT-HANDOFF\",\n      \"locator\": \"AR-036\",\n      \"basis\": \"User-selected current handoff and selective retention refinement. Reuse existing identity and responsibility; no runtime adoption or independent approval is asserted.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:7556595e9b9727f01d9dc27844d6bdc2a35ab5fac7a3c300a3b7baaaac3c0fbb","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-082-require-one-whole-change-review-gate-after-checked-implementation/AR-036-maintain-whole-change-review-standing-and-applicability.json"},"limitations":["Design assessment only; no runtime implementation, verification, executed adoption, package qualification or external-action authority is claimed.","Current source entrypoints, installed capabilities, project-selected authority and supported recording are distinct. A portable invocation cannot bypass an applicable governed contract; malformed governance is not permission to fall back.","Adoption requires compatible recording for selected work. Established new projects need no historical import; compatible work still needs authority/dependency checks; necessary unavailable migration blocks affected activation while preserving actual authority and history."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-036","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 3 canonical AR-036 criteria; integrated Design contribution with explicit failure, ownership and applicability limits.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:05f2cf53125f83fca4a85ab6c25c6d9cda699e20d20732a7042dc2730cb7accc","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:396489911ab6101e34638b257c875effad9895cb87ef711fe29615d114e5d238","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:dc2586d2d4c135693a8d8211f244133a9430a37c68173b25b7943a59c8782684","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:a08e94ba682a7f58b320393b65b538cea19758b5c069e02a91ed7a4f85753b0b","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/realization/software.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:bb60b1073280d894443e6098e497bc163800f43fbb3c08f8e55d09bb4ee36336","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-008-applicable-engineering-authoring-guidance/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c5f2bacaea51dbddc3bb23988c2cf98b8850770b8e7ba99cee8884191e8e0dc3","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-009-applicable-governed-action-authority/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a40e99dcc2b2ef9df4d63cd83064a726ebc2b76d2e045588cbbd59551e295332","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-010-claim-evidence-applicability-and-coverage/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:41e4298457e86fe690b4027327571f75c8e8cb98e10468f4ae157e3dbac31dd0","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-011-engineering-work-context-and-workflow-adoption/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:965b1f491fd98cb1864153f13d0a52ae73877ec5b8485bccbe4a670e02876e36","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-014-assurance-content-preparation/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a52db28adb589ab258420815dfaccfc743876128145cd62404c5df7968eee51b","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-029-assess-evidence-applicability-to-a-declared-claim.json"},{"identity":"sha256:85db55d933a26a2b6840d630caab1172dc9c820486bfca845444ab3fdf81fc59","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-030-expose-claim-criterion-coverage-and-contradictory-evidence.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cdfb0de0bee02ac23889aec83011b1f10878f8f15f03afef1e50648b8b184381","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-031-record-scoped-engineering-judgments-and-their-basis.json"},{"identity":"sha256:37cda3d53b5041ac563370cfb00effc0c5b2fc3d51c3af5273249e9061af9e4c","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9b77090a51b9d33af6a038261e36743682bca6b5cad4b293b99bb1989c2c3e36","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:fc6351e15674dd1cd14b07972e3b89f57756758294b2c2a10cf3483a562180ae","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:966ab13210fd36f3c44388d748827a1e36e1e2a6dc3b58b83f7afe46da077beb","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/workflow.md"},{"identity":"sha256:33306e44a1bd0ae1eae9b7b51c30dcf6bd261619207069e6974a6b3496864572","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d9bef4aadbfd845fc788a4e81a8c9ffb6f33cc7225a6d0acdd72d0e1992ef80f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:62bcaa4c905652e7287c4419c4f7a3422016c6d4f84b2b0a2782b0087c1bce12","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assessment.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9f6b3398a5cbbbc67e9cf98d2daf5d23978ac5174e8275983b0f39bab9af1481","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assurance-content.md"},{"identity":"sha256:43b41da458486e4bedc4801aee579e6de43d62f6527821ad0f7167d01240ce10","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-008-engineering-authoring-guidance/guidance.md"},{"identity":"sha256:bb597226b2064d47ab81b5ccfb4b8f97c1232ac72384a858a928362901432e6b","path":"CONSTITUTION.md"},{"identity":"sha256:b1f763a877947390ed6a24448c159dd370da5b341fbeca38e090291360c20a08","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-082-require-one-whole-change-review-gate-after-checked-implementation/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered within the stated contribution; no implementation or verification conclusion."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-012 advances eligible authorized milestones on completed required checks/dependencies rather than mandatory review handoffs.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"The complete implementation and cross-milestone interactions enter one independent whole-change gate; last-milestone or advisory scope cannot substitute.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Corrections remain in the same gate and final Verify requires current adequate approval; isolated work and optional PR keep their authority limits.","number":3,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-037\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Coordinate one whole change gate after implementation\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Skill procedures Module shall coordinate one whole change gate after implementation within its accountable boundary so that SR-082 can be satisfied without transferring another owner's decisions or state authority.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"The SR-082 obligation crosses guidance, governance or publication boundaries; an unowned contribution can make a locally valid step appear sufficient for the whole workflow.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Continue eligible authorized milestones after required checks without mandatory milestone review handoffs.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"MOD-012 owns the behavior or state needed for this contribution; separating it preserves one accountable owner while allowing the parent SR to compose several contributors.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Participants relying on Skill procedures\",\n        \"Authors, reviewers and project decision owners\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When the selected requirement-first workflow exercises SR-082 or reassesses its affected basis.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The MOD-012 responsibility boundary and its declared logical Interfaces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the allocated criteria through the constrained Functions and explicit contract inputs/outcomes; preserve actual actor decisions, subject identity and known limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocated contribution to SR-082; other contributors, independent assessment, physical recording implementation and product activation remain distinct.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Continue eligible authorized milestones after required checks without mandatory milestone review handoffs.\",\n    \"Send complete implementation, including cross-milestone interactions, to one formal whole-change gate; advisory feedback and a last-milestone-only review cannot substitute.\",\n    \"Route corrections within the same gate and require current adequate approval before final Verify; isolated scope and optional PR authority remain bounded.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The selected project contract, scope and required counterpart contributions are identifiable; absence is reported rather than inferred.\"\n  ],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"This draft allocation neither activates replacement runtime contracts nor proves implementation or satisfaction.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-012\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-053\",\n    \"FUNC-054\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-082; AR-037\",\n      \"basis\": \"Draft integrated design from the accepted requirement-first basis. This defines target responsibility and cooperation, not installed capability, design approval, runtime evidence or SQLite adoption.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:59c1c7ea19e6b103c8fe13ad2cbd0267dadb5088e5507d6cadd63d4b4a47caad","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-082-require-one-whole-change-review-gate-after-checked-implementation/AR-037-coordinate-one-whole-change-gate-after-implementation.json"},"limitations":["Design assessment only; no runtime implementation, verification, executed adoption, package qualification or external-action authority is claimed.","Current source entrypoints, installed capabilities, project-selected authority and supported recording are distinct. A portable invocation cannot bypass an applicable governed contract; malformed governance is not permission to fall back.","Adoption requires compatible recording for selected work. Established new projects need no historical import; compatible work still needs authority/dependency checks; necessary unavailable migration blocks affected activation while preserving actual authority and history."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-037","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 3 canonical AR-037 criteria; integrated Design contribution with explicit failure, ownership and applicability limits.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:05f2cf53125f83fca4a85ab6c25c6d9cda699e20d20732a7042dc2730cb7accc","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:396489911ab6101e34638b257c875effad9895cb87ef711fe29615d114e5d238","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:dc2586d2d4c135693a8d8211f244133a9430a37c68173b25b7943a59c8782684","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:a08e94ba682a7f58b320393b65b538cea19758b5c069e02a91ed7a4f85753b0b","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/realization/software.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:bb60b1073280d894443e6098e497bc163800f43fbb3c08f8e55d09bb4ee36336","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-008-applicable-engineering-authoring-guidance/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c5f2bacaea51dbddc3bb23988c2cf98b8850770b8e7ba99cee8884191e8e0dc3","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-009-applicable-governed-action-authority/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a40e99dcc2b2ef9df4d63cd83064a726ebc2b76d2e045588cbbd59551e295332","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-010-claim-evidence-applicability-and-coverage/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:41e4298457e86fe690b4027327571f75c8e8cb98e10468f4ae157e3dbac31dd0","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-011-engineering-work-context-and-workflow-adoption/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:965b1f491fd98cb1864153f13d0a52ae73877ec5b8485bccbe4a670e02876e36","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-014-assurance-content-preparation/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:aa83665c5155a32aa129ebb62e1179f03935efc4cb3b6a06613fe709deb02211","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-053-guide-a-bounded-specialist-engineering-activity.json"},{"identity":"sha256:72ed79db6e5aabe502b0d82ce6215409a69dfb1610502dcd458250607f97ba1a","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-054-determine-an-applicable-engineering-handoff.json"},{"identity":"sha256:37cda3d53b5041ac563370cfb00effc0c5b2fc3d51c3af5273249e9061af9e4c","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9b77090a51b9d33af6a038261e36743682bca6b5cad4b293b99bb1989c2c3e36","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:fc6351e15674dd1cd14b07972e3b89f57756758294b2c2a10cf3483a562180ae","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:966ab13210fd36f3c44388d748827a1e36e1e2a6dc3b58b83f7afe46da077beb","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/workflow.md"},{"identity":"sha256:33306e44a1bd0ae1eae9b7b51c30dcf6bd261619207069e6974a6b3496864572","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d9bef4aadbfd845fc788a4e81a8c9ffb6f33cc7225a6d0acdd72d0e1992ef80f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:62bcaa4c905652e7287c4419c4f7a3422016c6d4f84b2b0a2782b0087c1bce12","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assessment.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9f6b3398a5cbbbc67e9cf98d2daf5d23978ac5174e8275983b0f39bab9af1481","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assurance-content.md"},{"identity":"sha256:43b41da458486e4bedc4801aee579e6de43d62f6527821ad0f7167d01240ce10","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-008-engineering-authoring-guidance/guidance.md"},{"identity":"sha256:bb597226b2064d47ab81b5ccfb4b8f97c1232ac72384a858a928362901432e6b","path":"CONSTITUTION.md"},{"identity":"sha256:b1f763a877947390ed6a24448c159dd370da5b341fbeca38e090291360c20a08","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-082-require-one-whole-change-review-gate-after-checked-implementation/sr.json"}],"summary":"Design Covered within the stated contribution; no implementation or verification conclusion."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"FUNC-078 and IF-011 prepare explicit selected active-work and consumer dispositions, retaining original assessments, unresolved blockers and exact current bases.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Activation requires coherent actual compatibility and a fresh inspected basis; partial installation/transition reports intact versus unavailable authority and preserves recoverable work.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"MOD-006/FUNC-078 prepares a current dependency-specific disposition through IF-011, including established absence rather than fabricated current identity for a new project. Necessary legacy migration must be qualified before activation; unavailable or uncertain results withhold adoption. The Governance table and storage cooperation preserve work, original judgment identity and actual prior authority, reject empty-store substitution and avoid unrelated import.","number":3,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-038\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Reconcile bounded workflow adoption and recovery\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Change control Module shall reconcile bounded workflow adoption and recovery within its accountable boundary so that SR-083 can be satisfied without transferring another owner's decisions or state authority.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"The SR-083 obligation crosses guidance, governance or publication boundaries; an unowned contribution can make a locally valid step appear sufficient for the whole workflow. Treating migration as either universally mandatory or universally independent can misclassify selected work and lose its required historical support.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Prepare explicit dispositions for every affected active Change and dependency within the selected scope, retaining original review meanings.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"MOD-006 owns the behavior or state needed for this contribution; separating it preserves one accountable owner while allowing the parent SR to compose several contributors.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Participants relying on Change control\",\n        \"Authors, reviewers and project decision owners\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When the selected requirement-first workflow exercises SR-083 or reassesses its affected basis.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The MOD-006 responsibility boundary and its declared logical Interfaces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the allocated criteria through the constrained Functions and explicit contract inputs/outcomes; preserve actual actor decisions, subject identity and known limitations. Prepare the dependency-specific migration disposition before any activation decision; storage qualification and physical migration remain with their existing owners.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocated contribution to SR-083; other contributors, independent assessment, physical recording implementation and product activation remain distinct. Include the three SR-083 recording-compatibility cases and preserve unresolved dependent work without importing unrelated history.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Prepare explicit dispositions for every affected active Change and dependency within the selected scope, retaining original review meanings.\",\n    \"Require coherent consumer/recording support and a fresh adoption basis; interrupted or partial transition reports actual active authority and preserves recoverable work.\",\n    \"Determine whether selected work depends on incompatible earlier records. Require qualified migration for those dependencies before activation; new projects without earlier records need no historical import, and compatible existing work still needs fresh authority and dependency checks. Unavailable necessary migration blocks affected adoption. Preserve actual active authority, work and relied-on historical material; neither empty replacement records nor unrelated historical import discharges those obligations.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The selected project contract, scope and required counterpart contributions are identifiable; absence is reported rather than inferred.\"\n  ],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"This draft allocation neither activates replacement runtime contracts nor proves implementation or satisfaction.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-006\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-078\",\n    \"FUNC-023\",\n    \"FUNC-024\",\n    \"FUNC-025\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-083; AR-038\",\n      \"basis\": \"Draft integrated design from the accepted requirement-first basis. This defines target responsibility and cooperation, not installed capability, design approval, runtime evidence or SQLite adoption.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-ADOPTION-DEPENDENCY-REFINEMENT\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-083; SCN-082; AR-038; FUNC-078\",\n      \"basis\": \"Refine the existing adoption responsibility to distinguish new, compatible and migration-dependent selected work. Necessary migration is an activation dependency; unsupported, absent or stale facts never imply successful adoption. Preserve original subjects, authority, custody and qualified successor ownership; target Design only.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:c5d13d14f623676911bc02a08ffb5ef06c5b8229abe59c6635e6c2ed37381a74","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-083-adopt-replacement-workflow-contracts-without-reinterpreting-history/AR-038-reconcile-bounded-workflow-adoption-and-recovery.json"},"limitations":["Design assessment only; no runtime implementation, verification, executed adoption, package qualification or external-action authority is claimed.","Current source entrypoints, installed capabilities, project-selected authority and supported recording are distinct. A portable invocation cannot bypass an applicable governed contract; malformed governance is not permission to fall back.","Adoption requires compatible recording for selected work. Established new projects need no historical import; compatible work still needs authority/dependency checks; necessary unavailable migration blocks affected activation while preserving actual authority and history."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-038","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 3 canonical AR-038 criteria; integrated Design contribution with explicit failure, ownership and applicability limits.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:05f2cf53125f83fca4a85ab6c25c6d9cda699e20d20732a7042dc2730cb7accc","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:396489911ab6101e34638b257c875effad9895cb87ef711fe29615d114e5d238","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:dc2586d2d4c135693a8d8211f244133a9430a37c68173b25b7943a59c8782684","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:a08e94ba682a7f58b320393b65b538cea19758b5c069e02a91ed7a4f85753b0b","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/realization/software.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:bb60b1073280d894443e6098e497bc163800f43fbb3c08f8e55d09bb4ee36336","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-008-applicable-engineering-authoring-guidance/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c5f2bacaea51dbddc3bb23988c2cf98b8850770b8e7ba99cee8884191e8e0dc3","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-009-applicable-governed-action-authority/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a40e99dcc2b2ef9df4d63cd83064a726ebc2b76d2e045588cbbd59551e295332","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-010-claim-evidence-applicability-and-coverage/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:41e4298457e86fe690b4027327571f75c8e8cb98e10468f4ae157e3dbac31dd0","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-011-engineering-work-context-and-workflow-adoption/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:965b1f491fd98cb1864153f13d0a52ae73877ec5b8485bccbe4a670e02876e36","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-014-assurance-content-preparation/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8d5fd4b8c33d938deca10af6cfb9ae6cc22a2e554a02d2b62b0b9c737851eb5f","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-078-prepare-and-reconcile-workflow-adoption.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8985e5e5c42ec020c0b2d188d84ad38fb9e11a68701cf956767f9dc9e5cd3304","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-023-record-controlled-change-transitions-and-provenance.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a1950aba542f169c423b1352b1533716ef92894a540bf9c339a02f2a5d908de4","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-024-assess-and-apply-retirement-of-current-view-material.json"},{"identity":"sha256:b5bbfbf03874ea29120c3443bd5efc8160f8cbbf230286fde5316d5fee495ef1","path":"design/system/functions/FUNC-025-retain-and-retrieve-activity-specific-change-context.json"},{"identity":"sha256:37cda3d53b5041ac563370cfb00effc0c5b2fc3d51c3af5273249e9061af9e4c","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9b77090a51b9d33af6a038261e36743682bca6b5cad4b293b99bb1989c2c3e36","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:fc6351e15674dd1cd14b07972e3b89f57756758294b2c2a10cf3483a562180ae","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:966ab13210fd36f3c44388d748827a1e36e1e2a6dc3b58b83f7afe46da077beb","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-006-engineering-change-control/workflow.md"},{"identity":"sha256:33306e44a1bd0ae1eae9b7b51c30dcf6bd261619207069e6974a6b3496864572","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d9bef4aadbfd845fc788a4e81a8c9ffb6f33cc7225a6d0acdd72d0e1992ef80f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:62bcaa4c905652e7287c4419c4f7a3422016c6d4f84b2b0a2782b0087c1bce12","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assessment.md"},{"identity":"sha256:9f6b3398a5cbbbc67e9cf98d2daf5d23978ac5174e8275983b0f39bab9af1481","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-007-engineering-verification-and-assurance/assurance-content.md"},{"identity":"sha256:43b41da458486e4bedc4801aee579e6de43d62f6527821ad0f7167d01240ce10","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/modules/MOD-008-engineering-authoring-guidance/guidance.md"},{"identity":"sha256:bb597226b2064d47ab81b5ccfb4b8f97c1232ac72384a858a928362901432e6b","path":"CONSTITUTION.md"},{"identity":"sha256:b506771574be31c9d33ef38b8f27fa5c83b03ceefdcf8975eecc405eadf634b6","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-083-adopt-replacement-workflow-contracts-without-reinterpreting-history/sr.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a46554a9d89539fa9c40f21bd4b1f58bede833ca148065554a9abd311a992c6f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-019-product-delivery/modules/MOD-013-product-package-production/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:d02da6a994a304a3b45c6fb6f7197efc3fbf9796e6487996c592ea9406404a08","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-019-product-delivery/modules/MOD-013-product-package-production/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8826cafce61e450491f674a84da5ba1bcc8717a2f3328f2e6a2db1c29bccce23","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-019-product-delivery/modules/MOD-014-verified-skill-installation/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:59d599b2614481294c8ba32be965dc82e9099e98d702e1d085fc71a4e2ce9c5f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-019-product-delivery/modules/MOD-014-verified-skill-installation/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:497bc4cddf19fe61749b013dc94d07190982d0331ca50e99a54c62b04b2309b2","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8b16ad56639575b8c7b13dc5afaa72aecc19a53b59d205e9e6961311543d8666","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:7c613a1991e886ef07d9c8232ad8a0c6e39706f15fc8811a73165ca7959b502f","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:ce3cf826ac64c9b18bd826f10edd84c42165a2d2942ea3cdcefc13667f8b2575","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:3456dd8482b1b09d027fcfb47f06ca254702c3b26558e044c390ec3281b45428","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-003-operational-record-access-and-publication/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:8f6e4111c20a920b850e63107c7b39cafc51685e45bd0e4c5d9b9e8e7e0247c1","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-010-engineering-command-interface/command-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:8acfe8a596f2e5c4542635113f4bddf7db03806cf50e748e287b161cac0e03e8","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-011-operational-record-persistence/record-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:97b6e7c46e0bcf4d0a9c623173659796be5d8838634b3de5339367e1907eca8f","path":"design/requirements/scenarios/SCN-082-adopt-the-requirement-first-workflow-for-active-work.json"},{"identity":"sha256:6d82acd0a1443577c34296308b2c0cddf22e29b7fbc5324ab52a759914a634fe","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-017-engineering-governance/test-design.md"},{"identity":"sha256:536af7f9e97979b7afd41f8f5b66296e6091a243f1dfd3f9019f0ed2d3554782","path":"design/requirements/sources.md"}],"summary":"Design Covered against the explicitly refined adoption obligation; original negative assessment is preserved. No implementation or verification conclusion."},{"actor":"requirements-design-review","allocation":null,"ar_children":null,"criteria":[{"explanation":"MOD-012 resolves one compatible canonical method/resource set for the adopted branch; obsolete proposal-first and replacement meanings cannot coexist as active routes.","number":1,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Governed recording uses actual supported tasks; attributable document authority may cover its explicit scope only, never a fallback from malformed governed state or an invented general adoption exception.","number":2,"state":"covered"},{"explanation":"Stage-specific readiness, structure, installed availability and authority remain distinct, with specialist methods and isolated invocation boundaries preserved.","number":3,"state":"covered"}],"definition":{"content":"{\n  \"id\": \"AR-039\",\n  \"type\": \"allocated-requirement\",\n  \"title\": \"Use a coherent adopted workflow through supported capabilities\",\n  \"status\": \"draft\",\n  \"statement\": \"The Skill procedures Module shall use a coherent adopted workflow through supported capabilities within its accountable boundary so that SR-083 can be satisfied without transferring another owner's decisions or state authority.\",\n  \"analysis\": {\n    \"method\": \"5W2H\",\n    \"what\": {\n      \"problem\": \"The SR-083 obligation crosses guidance, governance or publication boundaries; an unowned contribution can make a locally valid step appear sufficient for the whole workflow.\",\n      \"desired_outcome\": \"Resolve one compatible canonical method and generated guidance set; do not expose old proposal-first and replacement meanings as concurrent valid routes.\"\n    },\n    \"why\": {\n      \"rationale\": \"MOD-012 owns the behavior or state needed for this contribution; separating it preserves one accountable owner while allowing the parent SR to compose several contributors.\"\n    },\n    \"who\": {\n      \"stakeholders\": [\n        \"Participants relying on Skill procedures\",\n        \"Authors, reviewers and project decision owners\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"when\": {\n      \"conditions\": [\n        \"When the selected requirement-first workflow exercises SR-083 or reassesses its affected basis.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"where\": {\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"The MOD-012 responsibility boundary and its declared logical Interfaces.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"how\": {\n      \"approach\": \"Apply the allocated criteria through the constrained Functions and explicit contract inputs/outcomes; preserve actual actor decisions, subject identity and known limitations.\"\n    },\n    \"how_much\": {\n      \"scope\": \"This allocated contribution to SR-083; other contributors, independent assessment, physical recording implementation and product activation remain distinct.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"Resolve one compatible canonical method and generated guidance set; do not expose old proposal-first and replacement meanings as concurrent valid routes.\",\n    \"Use only supported CLI operations for governed recording; document-based work is allowed only under explicit applicable project authority.\",\n    \"Keep stage-specific readiness distinct from schema validity and installation, preserving specialist and isolated invocation boundaries.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The selected project contract, scope and required counterpart contributions are identifiable; absence is reported rather than inferred.\"\n  ],\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"This draft allocation neither activates replacement runtime contracts nor proves implementation or satisfaction.\"\n  ],\n  \"allocated_to\": \"MOD-012\",\n  \"constrains\": [\n    \"FUNC-051\",\n    \"FUNC-052\",\n    \"FUNC-055\"\n  ],\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"SRC-WORKFLOW-DESIGN\",\n      \"locator\": \"SR-083; AR-039\",\n      \"basis\": \"Draft integrated design from the accepted requirement-first basis. This defines target responsibility and cooperation, not installed capability, design approval, runtime evidence or SQLite adoption.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","identity":"sha256:68d3bc974117e86fe6e691ab8562f676bfc9b709840da5a73a74e1f753a394ee","path":"design/requirements/IR-009-carry-out-portable-guided-engineering-work-across-the-project-lifecycle/SR-083-adopt-replacement-workflow-contracts-without-reinterpreting-history/AR-039-use-a-coherent-adopted-workflow-through-supported-capabilities.json"},"limitations":["Design assessment only; no runtime implementation, verification, executed adoption, package qualification or external-action authority is claimed.","Current source entrypoints, installed capabilities, project-selected authority and supported recording are distinct. A portable invocation cannot bypass an applicable governed contract; malformed governance is not permission to fall back.","Adoption requires compatible recording for selected work. Established new projects need no historical import; compatible work still needs authority/dependency checks; necessary unavailable migration blocks affected activation while preserving actual authority and history."],"outcome_basis":null,"reported_at":"2026-10-06T07:59:52Z","requirement":"AR-039","review":{"change":"2026-10-04-system-requirements-view-design","id":"ir010-integrated-design"},"scope":"All 3 canonical AR-039 criteria; integrated Design contribution with explicit failure, ownership and applicability limits.","state":"covered","subjects":[{"identity":"sha256:05f2cf53125f83fca4a85ab6c25c6d9cda699e20d20732a7042dc2730cb7accc","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/module.json"},{"identity":"sha256:396489911ab6101e34638b257c875effad9895cb87ef711fe29615d114e5d238","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:dc2586d2d4c135693a8d8211f244133a9430a37c68173b25b7943a59c8782684","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/capability-contract.md"},{"identity":"sha256:a08e94ba682a7f58b320393b65b538cea19758b5c069e02a91ed7a4f85753b0b","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/modules/MOD-012-published-engineering-capability-guidance/realization/software.json"},{"identity":"sha256:cd8d9be56ab4874f55cff54168f1cf3cc693de2bc40c17baf0dd034b4b2fd9c5","path":"design/architecture/modules/MOD-018-engineering-operations/README.md"},{"identity":"sha256:57770a58d93ee0bb6b875cb4de871a43ba33811dfe85b6205c2440a433e86623","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-004-scoped-public-command-execution/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:bb60b1073280d894443e6098e497bc163800f43fbb3c08f8e55d09bb4ee36336","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-008-applicable-engineering-authoring-guidance/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:c5f2bacaea51dbddc3bb23988c2cf98b8850770b8e7ba99cee8884191e8e0dc3","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-009-applicable-governed-action-authority/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:a40e99dcc2b2ef9df4d63cd83064a726ebc2b76d2e045588cbbd59551e295332","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-010-claim-evidence-applicability-and-coverage/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:41e4298457e86fe690b4027327571f75c8e8cb98e10468f4ae157e3dbac31dd0","path":"design/architecture/interfaces/IF-011-engineering-work-context-and-workflow-adoption/interface.json"},{"identity":"sha256:965b1f491fd98cb1864153f13d0a52ae73877ec5b8485bccbe4a670e02876e36","pa